msgid "Key to the Dependency Graph"
msgstr "ຄຳອະທິບາຍແຜນພູມຄວາມສຳພັນ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:17
msgid "3D boxes are hardware design variables or constraints"
msgstr "ກ່ອງ 3D ແມ່ນຕົວປ່ຽນ ຫຼື ຂໍ້ຈຳກັດດ້ານການອອກແບບຮາດແວ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:18
msgid "Oval-shaped boxes are software or system design variables or constraints"
msgstr "ກ່ອງຮູບວົງມົນແມ່ນຕົວປ່ຽນ ຫຼື ຂໍ້ຈຳກັດດ້ານການອອກແບບຊອບແວ ຫຼື ລະບົບ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:19
msgid ""
"Rectangle-shaped boxes are configurable parameters, color-coded by "
"configuration file:"
msgstr "ກ່ອງຮູບສີ່ຫຼ່ຽມແມ່ນພາຣາມິເຕີທີ່ສາມາດກຳນົດຄ່າໄດ້, ແບ່ງຕາມສີຂອງໄຟລ໌ກຳນົດຄ່າ:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:20
msgid "Red: Apache `httpd` configuration files"
msgstr "ສີແດງ: ໄຟລ໌ກຳນົດຄ່າ Apache `httpd`"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:21
msgid "Blue: Salt configuration files"
msgstr "ສີຟ້າ: ໄຟລ໌ກຳນົດຄ່າ Salt"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:22
msgid "Brown: Tomcat configuration files"
msgstr "ສີີນ້ຳຕານ: ໄຟລ໌ກຳນົດຄ່າ Tomcat"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:23
msgid "Grey: PostgreSQL configuration files"
msgstr "ສີເທົາ: ໄຟລ໌ກຳນົດຄ່າ PostgreSQL"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:24
msgid "Purple: `/etc/rhn/rhn.conf`"
msgstr "ສີມ່ວງ: `/etc/rhn/rhn.conf`"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:25
msgid ""
"Dashed connecting lines indicate a variable or constraint that might require "
"a change to another parameter"
msgstr "ເສັ້ນເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ແບບຂີດປະ ບົ່ງບອກເຖິງຕົວປ່ຽນ ຫຼື ຂໍ້ຈຳກັດທີ່ອາດຈະຕ້ອງມີການປ່ຽນແປງພາຣາມິເຕີອື່ນ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:26
msgid ""
"Solid connecting lines indicate that changing a configuration parameter "
"requires checking another one to prevent issues"
msgstr "ເສັ້ນເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ແບບເສັ້ນທຶບ ບົ່ງບອກວ່າການປ່ຽນພາຣາມິເຕີກຳນົດຄ່າໜຶ່ງ ຕ້ອງມີການກວດສອບອີກອັນໜຶ່ງເພື່ອປ້ອງກັນບັນຫາ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:27
msgid ""
"After the initial tuning has been completed, you will need to consider "
"tuning again in these cases:"
msgstr "ຫຼັງຈາກການປັບແຕ່ງເບື້ອງຕົ້ນສຳເລັດແລ້ວ, ເຈົ້າຈະຕ້ອງພິຈາລະນາການປັບແຕ່ງຄືນໃໝ່ໃນກໍລະນີເຫຼົ່ານີ້:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:28
msgid "If your tuning inputs change significantly"
msgstr "ຫາກຂໍ້ມູນຕົວປ່ຽນໃນການປັບແຕ່ງມີການປ່ຽນແປງຢ່າງຫຼວງຫຼາຍ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:29
msgid "If special conditions arise that require a certain parameter to be changed."
msgstr "ຫາກມີເງື່ອນໄຂພິເສດທີ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ຕ້ອງປ່ຽນພາຣາມິເຕີບາງຢ່າງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:30
msgid "For example, if specific warnings appear in a log file."
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງ: ຫາກມີການແຈ້ງເຕືອນສະເພາະປາກົດຂຶ້ນໃນໄຟລ໌ log."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:31
msgid "If performance is not satisfactory"
msgstr "ຫາກປະສິດທິພາບບໍ່ເປັນທີ່ໜ້າພໍໃຈ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:32
msgid ""
"To re-tune your installation, you will need to use the dependency graph "
"again.  Start from the node where significant change has happened."
msgstr "ໃນການປັບແຕ່ງລະບົບຄືນໃໝ່, ເຈົ້າຈະຕ້ອງໃຊ້ແຜນພູມຄວາມສຳພັນອີກຄັ້ງ. ເລີ່ມຈາກໂນດທີ່ມີການປ່ຽນແປງທີ່ສຳຄັນເກີດຂຶ້ນ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "Environmental Variables"
msgstr "ຕົວປ່ຽນສະພາບແວດລ້ອມ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:34
msgid ""
"This section contains information about environmental variables (inputs to "
"the tuning process)."
msgstr "ພາກນີ້ປະກອບດ້ວຍຂໍ້ມູນກ່ຽວກັບຕົວປ່ຽນສະພາບແວດລ້ອມ (ຂໍ້ມູນນຳເຂົ້າສຳລັບຂະບວນການປັບແຕ່ງ)."

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "Network Bandwidth"
msgstr "ແບນວິດເຄືອຂ່າຍ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:36
msgid ""
"A measure of the typically available egress bandwith from the {productname} "
"Server host to the clients or {productname} Proxy hosts.  This should take "
"into account network hardware and topology as well as possible capacity "
"limits on switches, routers, and other network equipment between the server "
"and clients."
msgstr "ການວັດແທກແບນວິດຂາອອກ (egress bandwidth) ທີ່ສາມາດໃຊ້ໄດ້ຈາກເຄື່ອງ {productname} Server ໄປຫາໄຄລແອນ ຫຼື ເຄື່ອງ {productname} Proxy. ສິ່ງນີ້ຄວນພິຈາລະນາເຖິງຮາດແວເຄືອຂ່າຍ ແລະ ໂທໂປໂລຢີ ລວມທັງຂໍ້ຈຳກັດດ້ານຄວາມສາມາດຂອງ switch, router ແລະ ອຸປະກອນເຄືອຂ່າຍອື່ນໆ ລະຫວ່າງເຊີເວີ ແລະ ໄຄລແອນ."

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:37
#, no-wrap
msgid "Channel count"
msgstr "ຈຳນວນແຊນແນວ (Channel)"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:38
msgid ""
"The number of expected channels to manage.  Includes any vendor-provided, "
"third-party, and cloned or staged channels."
msgstr "ຈຳນວນແຊນແນວທີ່ຄາດວ່າຈະຈັດການ. ລວມເຖິງແຊນແນວທີ່ມາຈາກຜູ້ຜະລິດ (vendor), ພາກສ່ວນທີສາມ, ແລະ ແຊນແນວທີ່ຖືກໂຄລນ (cloned) ຫຼື ສະເຕຈ (staged)."

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:39
#, no-wrap
msgid "Client count"
msgstr "ຈຳນວນໄຄລແອນ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:40
msgid ""
"The total number of actual or expected clients.  It is important to tune any "
"parameters in advance of a client count increase, whenever possible."
msgstr "ຈຳນວນລວມຂອງໄຄລແອນທີ່ມີຢູ່ຈິງ ຫຼື ທີ່ຄາດໄວ້. ມັນສຳຄັນຫຼາຍທີ່ຕ້ອງປັບແຕ່ງພາຣາມິເຕີຕ່າງໆລ່ວງໜ້າກ່ອນທີ່ຈຳນວນໄຄລແອນຈະເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນ."

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:41
#, no-wrap
msgid "OS mix"
msgstr "ການປະສົມປະສານ OS"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:42
msgid ""
"The number of distinct operating system versions that managed clients have "
"installed.  This is ordered by family ({sle}, openSUSE, {rhel}, or {ubuntu} "
"based).  Storage and computing requirements are different in each case."
msgstr "ຈຳນວນເວີຊັນຂອງລະບົບປະຕິບັດການທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນເຊິ່ງໄຄລແອນທີ່ຢູ່ພາຍໃຕ້ການຈັດການໄດ້ຕິດຕັ້ງໄວ້. ສິ່ງນີ້ຖືກຈັດແບ່ງຕາມຕະກູນ (ອີງຕາມ {sle}, openSUSE, {rhel}, ຫຼື {ubuntu}). ຄວາມຕ້ອງການດ້ານພື້ນທີ່ຈັດເກັບ ແລະ ການປະມວນຜົນຈະແຕກຕ່າງກັນໃນແຕ່ລະກໍລະນີ."

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:43
#, no-wrap
msgid "User count"
msgstr "ຈຳນວນຜູ້ໃຊ້"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:44
msgid ""
"The expected maximum amount of concurrent users interacting with the {webui} "
"plus the number of programs simultaneously using the XMLRPC API.  Includes "
"`spacecmd`, `spacewalk-clone-by-date`, and similar."
msgstr "ຈຳນວນຜູ້ໃຊ້ສູງສຸດທີ່ຄາດວ່າຈະໃຊ້ງານ {webui} ພ້ອມໆກັນ ລວມທັງຈຳນວນໂປຣແກຣມທີ່ໃຊ້ XMLRPC API ໃນເວລາດຽວກັນ. ລວມເຖິງ `spacecmd`, `spacewalk-clone-by-date` ແລະ ອື່ນໆທີ່ຄ້າຍຄືກັນ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:45
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr "ພາຣາມິເຕີ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:46
msgid "This section contains information about the available parameters."
msgstr "ພາກນີ້ປະກອບດ້ວຍຂໍ້ມູນກ່ຽວກັບພາຣາມິເຕີຕ່າງໆທີ່ສາມາດໃຊ້ໄດ້."

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "`MaxClients`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:48
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The maximum number of HTTP requests served "
"simultaneously by Apache httpd.\n"
"                         Proxies, {webui}, and XMLRPC API clients each "
"consume one.\n"
"                         Requests exceeding the parameter will be queued and "
"might result in timeouts.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:user-count[User count] and proxy count "
"increase significantly and this line appears in "
"[path]``/var/log/apache2/error_log``: [systemitem]``[...] "
"[mpm_prefork:error] [pid ...] AH00161: server reached MaxRequestWorkers "
"setting, consider raising the MaxRequestWorkers setting``.\n"
"| Value default        | 150\n"
"| Value recommendation | 150-500\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/apache2/server-tuning.conf``, in the "
"`prefork.c` section\n"
"| Example              | `MaxClients = 200`\n"
"| After changing       | Immediately change xref:server-limit[`ServerLimit`] "
"and check xref:max-threads[`maxThreads`] for possible adjustment.\n"
"| Notes                | This parameter was renamed to `MaxRequestWorkers`, "
"both names are valid.\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.4/en/mod/mpm_common.html#maxrequestworkers\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:49
#, no-wrap
msgid "`ServerLimit`"
msgstr "`ServerLimit`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The number of Apache httpd processes serving HTTP "
"requests simultaneously.\n"
"                         The number must equal "
"xref:max-clients[`MaxClients`].\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:max-clients[`MaxClients`] changes\n"
"| Value default        | 150\n"
"| Value recommendation | The same value as xref:max-clients[`MaxClients`]\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/apache2/server-tuning.conf``, in the "
"`prefork.c` section\n"
"| Example              | `ServerLimit = 200`\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.4/en/mod/mpm_common.html#serverlimit\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "`maxThreads`"
msgstr "`maxThreads`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:52
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The number of Tomcat threads dedicated to serving "
"HTTP requests\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:max-clients[`MaxClients`] changes.\n"
"                         `maxThreads` must always be equal or greater than "
"xref:max-clients[`MaxClients`]\n"
"| Value default        | 150\n"
"| Value recommendation | The same value as xref:max-clients[`MaxClients`]\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/tomcat/server.xml``\n"
"| Example              | `<Connector port=\"8009\" protocol=\"AJP/1.3\" "
"redirectPort=\"8443\" URIEncoding=\"UTF-8\" address=\"127.0.0.1\" "
"maxThreads=\"200\" connectionTimeout=\"20000\"/>`\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://tomcat.apache.org/tomcat-9.0-doc/config/http.html\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:53
#, no-wrap
msgid "`connectionTimeout`"
msgstr "`connectionTimeout`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:54
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The number of milliseconds before a non-responding "
"AJP connection is forcibly closed.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] increases "
"significantly and ``AH00992``, ``AH00877``, and ``AH01030`` errors appear in "
"Apache error logs during a load peak.\n"
"| Value default        | 900000\n"
"| Value recommendation | 20000-3600000\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/tomcat/server.xml``\n"
"| Example              | `<Connector port=\"8009\" protocol=\"AJP/1.3\" "
"redirectPort=\"8443\" URIEncoding=\"UTF-8\" address=\"127.0.0.1\" "
"maxThreads=\"200\" connectionTimeout=\"1000000\" "
"keepAliveTimeout=\"300000\"/>`\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://tomcat.apache.org/tomcat-9.0-doc/config/http.html\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "`keepAliveTimeout`"
msgstr "`keepAliveTimeout`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:56
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The number of milliseconds without data exchange "
"from the JVM before a non-responding AJP connection is forcibly closed.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] increases "
"significantly and ``AH00992``, ``AH00877``, and ``AH01030`` errors appear in "
"Apache error logs during a load peak.\n"
"| Value default        | 300000\n"
"| Value recommendation | 20000-600000\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/tomcat/server.xml``\n"
"| Example              | `<Connector port=\"8009\" protocol=\"AJP/1.3\" "
"redirectPort=\"8443\" URIEncoding=\"UTF-8\" address=\"127.0.0.1\" "
"maxThreads=\"200\" connectionTimeout=\"1000000\" "
"keepAliveTimeout=\"400000\"/>`\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://tomcat.apache.org/tomcat-9.0-doc/config/http.html\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:57
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tomcat's `-Xmx`"
msgstr "Tomcat's `-Xmx`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:58
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The maximum amount of memory Tomcat can use\n"
"| Tune when            | "
"xref:java-message-queue-thread-pool-size[`java.message_queue_thread_pool_size`] "
"is increased or\n"
"`OutOfMemoryException` errors appear in `/var/log/rhn/rhn_web_ui.log`\n"
"| Value default        | 1{nbsp}GiB\n"
"| Value recommendation | 4-8{nbsp}GiB\n"
"| Location             | "
"[path]``/etc/tomcat/conf.d/tomcat_java_opts.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `JAVA_OPTS=\"... -Xmx8G ...\"`\n"
"| After changing       | Check xref:memory-usage[memory usage]\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://docs.oracle.com/javase/8/docs/technotes/tools/windows/java.html\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:59
#, no-wrap
msgid "`java.disable_list_update_status`"
msgstr "`java.disable_list_update_status`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:60
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Disable displaying the update status for clients of "
"a system group\n"
"| Tune when            | displaying the update status causes timeouts\n"
"| Value default        | `false`\n"
"| Value recommendation | \n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `java.disable_list_update_status = true`\n"
"| After changing       | ?\n"
"| Notes                |\n"
"| More information     | `man rhn.conf`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "`java.message_queue_thread_pool_size`"
msgstr "`java.message_queue_thread_pool_size`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:62
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The maximum number of threads in Tomcat dedicated "
"to asynchronous operations\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] increases "
"significantly\n"
"| Value default        | 5\n"
"| Value recommendation | 50 - 150\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `java.message_queue_thread_pool_size = 50`\n"
"| After changing       | Check "
"xref:hibernate-c3p0-max-size[`hibernate.c3p0.max_size`], as each thread "
"consumes a PostgreSQL connection, starvation might happen if the allocated "
"connection pool is insufficient.\n"
"                         Check xref:thread-pool[`thread_pool`], as each "
"thread might perform Salt API calls, starvation might happen if the "
"allocated Salt thread pool is insufficient.\n"
"                         Check xref:tomcat-xmx[Tomcat's `-Xmx`], as each "
"thread consumes memory, `OutOfMemoryException` might be raised if "
"insufficient.\n"
"| Notes                | Incoming Salt events are handled in separate thread "
"pool, see "
"xref:java-salt-event-thread-pool-size[`java.salt_event_thread_pool_size`]\n"
"| More information     | `man rhn.conf`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:63
#, no-wrap
msgid "`java.salt_batch_size`"
msgstr "`java.salt_batch_size`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:64
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The maximum number of minions concurrently "
"executing a scheduled action.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] reaches several "
"thousands and actions are not executed quickly enough.\n"
"| Value default        | 200\n"
"| Value recommendation | 200-500\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `java.salt_batch_size = 300`\n"
"| After changing       | Check xref:memory-usage[memory usage].\n"
"                         Monitor memory usage closely before and after the "
"change.\n"
"| More information     | "
"xref:specialized-guides:salt/salt-rate-limiting.adoc[Salt Rate Limiting]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:65
#, no-wrap
msgid "`java.salt_event_thread_pool_size`"
msgstr "`java.salt_event_thread_pool_size`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The maximum number of threads in Tomcat dedicated "
"to handling of incoming Salt events.\n"
"| Tune when            | The number of queued Salt events grows. Typically, "
"this can happen during onboarding of large number of minions with higher "
"value of\n"
"                         "
"xref:java-salt-presence-ping-timeout[`java.salt_presence_ping_timeout`].\n"
"                         The number of events can be queried by "
"[command]``echo \"select count(*) from susesaltevent;\" \\| spacewalk-sql "
"--select-mode-direct - ``\n"
"| Value default        | 8\n"
"| Value recommendation | 20-100\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `java.salt_event_thread_pool_size = 50`\n"
"| After changing       | Check the length of Salt event queue.\n"
"                         Check "
"xref:hibernate-c3p0-max-size[`hibernate.c3p0.max_size`], as each thread "
"consumes a PostgreSQL connection, starvation might happen if the allocated "
"connection pool is insufficient.\n"
"                         Check xref:thread-pool[`thread_pool`], as each "
"thread might perform Salt API calls, starvation might happen if the "
"allocated Salt thread pool is insufficient.\n"
"                         Check xref:tomcat-xmx[Tomcat's `-Xmx`], as each "
"thread consumes memory, `OutOfMemoryException` might be raised if "
"insufficient.\n"
"| More information     | `man rhn.conf`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:67
#, no-wrap
msgid "`java.salt_presence_ping_timeout`"
msgstr "`java.salt_presence_ping_timeout`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:68
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Before any action is executed on a client, a "
"presence ping is executed to make sure the client is reachable.\n"
"                         This parameter sets the amount of time before a "
"second command (in most cases `state.apply` or any other {salt} function) is "
"sent to the client to verify its presence.\n"
"                         Having many clients typically means some will "
"respond faster than others, so this timeout could be raised to accommodate "
"for the slower ones.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] increases "
"significantly, or some clients are responding correctly but too slowly, and "
"{productname} excludes them from calls.\n"
"                         This line appears in "
"[path]``/var/log/rhn/rhn_web_ui.log``: [systemitem]``\"Got no result for "
"<COMMAND> on minion <MINION_ID> (minion did not respond in time)\"``\n"
"| Value default        | 4 seconds\n"
"| Value recommendation | 4-20 seconds\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `java.salt_presence_ping_timeout = 10`\n"
"| After changing       | Large `java.salt_presence_ping_timeout` value can "
"reduce overall throughput.\n"
"                         This can be compensated by increasing "
"xref:java-salt-event-thread-pool-size[`java.salt_event_thread_pool_size`]\n"
"| More information     | "
"xref:specialized-guides:salt/salt-timeouts.adoc[Salt Timeouts]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:69
#, no-wrap
msgid "`java.salt_presence_ping_gather_job_timeout`"
msgstr "`java.salt_presence_ping_gather_job_timeout`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:70
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Before any action is executed on a client, a "
"presence ping is executed to make sure the client is reachable.\n"
"                         After "
"xref:java-salt-presence-ping-timeout[`java.salt_presence_ping_timeout`] "
"seconds have elapsed without a response, a second command (in most cases "
"`state.apply` or any other {salt} function) is sent to the client and if "
"there is no response from the client for the amount of seconds specified "
"with this parameter one more call (`saltutil.find_job`) is sent for a final "
"check.\n"
"                         This parameter sets the number of seconds after the "
"second command after which the client is definitely considered timeout.\n"
"                         Having many clients typically means some will "
"respond faster than others, so this timeout could be raised to accommodate "
"for the slower ones.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] increases "
"significantly, or some clients are responding correctly but too slowly, and "
"{productname} excludes them from calls.\n"
"                         This line appears in "
"[path]``/var/log/rhn/rhn_web_ui.log``: [systemitem]``\"Got no result for "
"<COMMAND> on minion <MINION_ID> (minion did not respond in time)\"``\n"
"| Value default        | 1 second\n"
"| Value recommendation | 1-50 seconds\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `java.salt_presence_ping_gather_job_timeout = 20`\n"
"| More information     | "
"xref:specialized-guides:salt/salt-timeouts.adoc[Salt Timeouts]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:71
#, no-wrap
msgid "`java.taskomatic_channel_repodata_workers`"
msgstr "`java.taskomatic_channel_repodata_workers`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:72
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Whenever content is changed in a software channel, "
"its metadata needs to be recomputed before clients can use it.\n"
"                         Channel-altering operations include the addition of "
"a patch, the removal of a package or a repository synchronization run.\n"
"                         This parameter specifies the maximum number of "
"Taskomatic threads that {productname} will use to recompute the channel "
"metadata.\n"
"                         Channel metadata computation is both CPU-bound and "
"memory-heavy, so raising this parameter and operating on many channels "
"simultaneously could cause Taskomatic to consume significant resources, but "
"channels will be available to clients sooner.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:channel-count[Channel count] becoms larger "
"than 50, or more concurrent operations on channels are expected.\n"
"| Value default        | 2\n"
"| Value recommendation | 2-10\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `java.taskomatic_channel_repodata_workers = 4`\n"
"| After changing       | Check "
"xref:taskomatic-java-maxmemory[`taskomatic.java.maxmemory`] for adjustment, "
"as every new thread will consume memory\n"
"| More information     | `man rhn.conf`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:73
#, no-wrap
msgid "`taskomatic.java.maxmemory`"
msgstr "`taskomatic.java.maxmemory`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:74
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The maximum amount of memory Taskomatic can use.\n"
"                         Generation of metadata, especially for some OSs, "
"can be memory-intensive, so this parameter might need raising depending on "
"the managed xref:os-mix[OS mix].\n"
"| Tune when            | "
"xref:java-taskomatic-channel-repodata-workers[`java.taskomatic_channel_repodata_workers`] "
"increases, OSs are added to {productname} (particularly {rhel} or {ubuntu}), "
"or `OutOfMemoryException` errors appear in "
"`/var/log/rhn/rhn_taskomatic_daemon.log`.\n"
"| Value default        | 4096 MiB\n"
"| Value recommendation | 4096-16384 MiB\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `taskomatic.java.maxmemory = 8192`\n"
"| After changing       | Check xref:memory-usage[memory usage].\n"
"| More information     | `man rhn.conf`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:75
#, no-wrap
msgid "`org.quartz.threadPool.threadCount`"
msgstr "`org.quartz.threadPool.threadCount`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The number of Taskomatic worker threads.\n"
"                         Increasing this value allows Taskomatic to serve "
"more clients in parallel.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] increases "
"significantly\n"
"| Value default        | 20\n"
"| Value recommendation | 20-200\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `org.quartz.threadPool.threadCount = 100`\n"
"| After changing       | Check "
"xref:hibernate-c3p0-max-size[`hibernate.c3p0.max_size`] and "
"xref:thread-pool[`thread_pool`] for adjustment\n"
"| More information     | "
"http://www.quartz-scheduler.org/documentation/2.4.0-SNAPSHOT/configuration.html\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:77
#, no-wrap
msgid "`org.quartz.scheduler.idleWaitTime`"
msgstr "`org.quartz.scheduler.idleWaitTime`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:78
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Cycle time for Taskomatic.\n"
"                         Decreasing this value lowers the latency of "
"Taskomatic.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] is in the "
"thousands.\n"
"| Value default        | 5000 ms\n"
"| Value recommendation | 1000-5000 ms\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `org.quartz.scheduler.idleWaitTime = 1000`\n"
"| More information     | "
"http://www.quartz-scheduler.org/documentation/2.4.0-SNAPSHOT/configuration.html\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:79
#, no-wrap
msgid "`MinionActionExecutor.parallel_threads`"
msgstr "`MinionActionExecutor.parallel_threads`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:80
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Number of Taskomatic threads dedicated to sending "
"commands to Salt clients as a result of actions being executed.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] is in the "
"thousands.\n"
"| Value default        | 1\n"
"| Value recommendation | 1-10\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `taskomatic.minion_action_executor.parallel_threads "
"= 10`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "`SSHMinionActionExecutor.parallel_threads`"
msgstr "`SSHMinionActionExecutor.parallel_threads`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:82
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Number of Taskomatic threads dedicated to sending "
"commands to Salt SSH clients as a result of actions being executed.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] is in the "
"hundreds.\n"
"| Value default        | 20\n"
"| Value recommendation | 20-100\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | "
"`taskomatic.sshminion_action_executor.parallel_threads = 40`\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:83
#, no-wrap
msgid "`hibernate.c3p0.max_size`"
msgstr "`hibernate.c3p0.max_size`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:84
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Maximum number of PostgreSQL connections "
"simultaneously available to both Tomcat and Taskomatic.\n"
"                         If any of those components requires more concurrent "
"connections, their requests will be queued.\n"
"| Tune when            | "
"xref:java-message-queue-thread-pool-size[`java.message_queue_thread_pool_size`] "
"or xref:max-threads[`maxThreads`] increase significantly, or when "
"xref:org-quartz-threadPool-threadCount[`org.quartz.threadPool.threadCount`] "
"has changed significantly.\n"
"                         Each thread consumes one connection in Taskomatic "
"and Tomcat, having more threads than connections might result in starving.\n"
"| Value default        | 20\n"
"| Value recommendation | 100 to 200, higher than the maximum of "
"xref:java-message-queue-thread-pool-size[`java.message_queue_thread_pool_size`] "
"+ xref:max-threads[`maxThreads`] and "
"xref:org-quartz-threadPool-threadCount[`org.quartz.threadPool.threadCount`]\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `hibernate.c3p0.max_size = 100`\n"
"| After changing       | Check xref:max-connections[`max_connections`] for "
"adjustment.\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://www.mchange.com/projects/c3p0/#maxPoolSize\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:85
#, no-wrap
msgid "`rhn-search.java.maxmemory`"
msgstr "`rhn-search.java.maxmemory`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The maximum amount of memory that the `rhn-search` "
"service can use.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] increases "
"significantly, and `OutOfMemoryException` errors appear in `journalctl -u "
"rhn-search`.\n"
"| Value default        | 512 MiB\n"
"| Value recommendation | 512-4096 MiB\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/rhn/rhn.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `rhn-search.java.maxmemory = 4096`\n"
"| After changing       | Check xref:memory-usage[memory usage].\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "`shared_buffers`"
msgstr "`shared_buffers`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:88
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The amount of memory reserved for PostgreSQL shared "
"buffers, which contain caches of database tables and index data.\n"
"| Tune when            | RAM changes\n"
"| Value default        | 25% of total RAM\n"
"| Value recommendation | 25-40% of total RAM\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/var/lib/pgsql/data/postgresql.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `shared_buffers = 8192MB`\n"
"| After changing       | Check xref:memory-usage[memory usage].\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/15/runtime-config-resource.html#GUC-SHARED-BUFFERS\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:89
#, no-wrap
msgid "`max_connections`"
msgstr "`max_connections`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:90
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Maximum number of PostgreSQL connections available "
"to applications.\n"
"                         More connections allow for more concurrent "
"threads/workers in various components (in particular Tomcat and Taskomatic), "
"which generally improves performance.\n"
"                         However, each connection consumes resources, in "
"particular xref:work-mem[`work_mem`] megabytes per sort operation per "
"connection.\n"
"| Tune when            | "
"xref:hibernate-c3p0-max-size[`hibernate.c3p0.max_size`] changes "
"significantly, as that parameter determines the maximum number of "
"connections available to Tomcat and Taskomatic\n"
"| Value default        | 400\n"
"| Value recommendation | Depends on other settings, use "
"[command]``/usr/lib/susemanager/bin/susemanager-connection-check`` to obtain "
"a recommendation.\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/var/lib/pgsql/data/postgresql.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `max_connections = 250`\n"
"| After changing       | Check xref:memory-usage[memory usage].\n"
"                         Monitor memory usage closely before and after the "
"change.\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/15/runtime-config-connection.html#GUC-MAX-CONNECTIONS\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "`work_mem`"
msgstr "`work_mem`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:92
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The amount of memory allocated by PostgreSQL every "
"time a connection needs to do a sort or hash operation.\n"
"                         Every connection (as specified by "
"xref:max-connections[`max_connections`]) might make use of an amount of "
"memory equal to a multiple of `work_mem`.\n"
"| Tune when            | Database operations are slow because of excessive "
"temporary file disk I/O.\n"
"To test if that is happening, add ``log_temp_files = 5120`` to "
"[path]``/var/lib/pgsql/data/postgresql.conf``, restart PostgreSQL, and "
"monitor the PostgreSQL log files.\n"
"If you see lines containing ``LOG:  temporary file:`` try raising this "
"parameter's value to help reduce disk I/O and speed up database "
"operations.\n"
"| Value recommendation | 2-20 MB\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/var/lib/pgsql/data/postgresql.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `work_mem = 10MB`\n"
"| After changing       | check if the {productname} Server might need "
"additional RAM.\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/15/runtime-config-resource.html#GUC-WORK-MEM\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:93
#, no-wrap
msgid "`effective_cache_size`"
msgstr "`effective_cache_size`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:94
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Estimation of the total memory available to "
"PostgreSQL for caching.\n"
"                         It is the explicitly reserved memory "
"(xref:shared-buffers[`shared_buffers`]) plus any memory used by the kernel "
"as cache/buffer.\n"
"| Tune when            | Hardware RAM or memory usage increase "
"significantly\n"
"| Value recommendation | Start with 75% of total RAM.\n"
"                         For finer settings, use "
"xref:shared-buffers[`shared_buffers`] + free memory + buffer/cache memory.\n"
"                         Free and buffer/cache can be determined via the "
"`free -m` command (`free` and `buff/cache` in the output respectively)\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/var/lib/pgsql/data/postgresql.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `effective_cache_size = 24GB`\n"
"| After changing       | Check xref:memory-usage[memory usage]\n"
"| Notes                | This is an estimation for the query planner, not an "
"allocation.\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://www.postgresql.org/docs/15/runtime-config-query.html#GUC-EFFECTIVE-CACHE-SIZE\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:95
#, no-wrap
msgid "`thread_pool`"
msgstr "`thread_pool`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:96
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The number of worker threads serving Salt API HTTP "
"requests.\n"
"                         A higher number can improve parallelism of "
"{productname} Server-initiated Salt operations, but will consume more "
"memory.\n"
"| Tune when            | "
"xref:java-message-queue-thread-pool-size[`java.message_queue_thread_pool_size`] "
"or "
"xref:org-quartz-threadPool-threadCount[`org.quartz.threadPool.threadCount`] "
"are changed.\n"
"                         Starvation can occur when there are more Tomcat or "
"Taskomatic threads making simultaneous Salt API calls than there are Salt "
"API worker threads.\n"
"| Value default        | 100\n"
"| Value recommendation | 100-500, but should be higher than the sum of "
"xref:java-message-queue-thread-pool-size[`java.message_queue_thread_pool_size`] "
"and "
"xref:org-quartz-threadPool-threadCount[`org.quartz.threadPool.threadCount`]\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/salt/master.d/susemanager.conf``, in "
"the `rest_cherrypy` section.\n"
"| Example              | `thread_pool: 100`\n"
"| After changing       | Check xref:worker-threads[`worker_threads`] for "
"adjustment.\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://docs.saltproject.io/en/latest/ref/netapi/all/salt.netapi.rest_cherrypy.html#performance-tuning\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "`worker_threads`"
msgstr "`worker_threads`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:98
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The number of `salt-master` worker threads that "
"process commands and replies from minions and the Salt API.\n"
"                         Increasing this value, assuming sufficient "
"resources are available, allows Salt to process more data in parallel from "
"minions without timing out, but will consume significantly more RAM "
"(typically about 70 MiB per thread).\n"
"                         Setting this value to very high values could cause "
"opposite effect as the workers will compete to each other for the CPU "
"resources and the performance could be dropped significantly.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] increases "
"significantly, xref:thread-pool[`thread_pool`] increases significantly, or "
"`SaltReqTimeoutError` or `Message timed out` errors appear in "
"`/var/log/salt/master` could be a sign of too low or too high value of this "
"parameter.\n"
"| Value default        | 8\n"
"| Value recommendation | 8-32, depending on the number of the CPU cores "
"available for the server, it is recommended to keep the value slightly less "
"than the number of CPU cores.\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/salt/master.d/tuning.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `worker_threads: 16`\n"
"| After changing       | Check xref:memory-usage[memory usage].\n"
"                         Monitor memory usage closely before and after the "
"change.\n"
"                         It makes sense to monitor the `salt-master` stats "
"event by enabling `master_stats` and adjusting `master_stats_event_iter` to "
"fine tune the value of this parameter.\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://docs.saltproject.io/en/latest/ref/configuration/master.html#worker-threads\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:99
#, no-wrap
msgid "`auth_events`"
msgstr "`auth_events`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:100
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Determines whether the master will fire "
"authentication events. Authentication events are fired when a minion "
"performs an authentication check with the master.\n"
"                         It helps to reduce the number of events published "
"with the Salt Master Event Publisher and reduce the workload on Event "
"Publisher subscribers.\n"
"| Tune when            | Large amount of `salt/auth` events published in the "
"Salt event bus, which in most cases are useless for the subscribers.\n"
"| Value default        | True\n"
"| Value recommendation | False\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/salt/master.d/tuning.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `auth_events: False`\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://docs.saltproject.io/en/latest/ref/configuration/master.html#auth-events\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:101
#, no-wrap
msgid "`minion_data_cache_events`"
msgstr "`minion_data_cache_events`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Determines whether the master will fire minion data "
"cache events (`minion/refresh/*`). Minion data cache events are fired when a "
"minion requests a minion data cache refresh.\n"
"                         It helps to reduce the number of events published "
"with the Salt Master Event Publisher and reduce the workload on Event "
"Publisher subscribers.\n"
"| Tune when            | Large amount of `minion/refresh/*` events published "
"in the Salt event bus, which in most cases are useless for the "
"subscribers.\n"
"| Value default        | True\n"
"| Value recommendation | False\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/salt/master.d/tuning.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `minion_data_cache_events: False`\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://docs.saltproject.io/en/latest/ref/configuration/master.html#minion-data-cache-events\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "`pub_hwm`"
msgstr "`pub_hwm`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:104
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The maximum number of outstanding messages sent by "
"`salt-master`. If more than this number of messages need to be sent "
"concurrently, communication with clients slows down, potentially resulting "
"in timeout errors during load peaks.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] increases "
"significantly and ``Salt request timed out. The master is not responding.`` "
"errors appear when pinging minions during a load peak.\n"
"| Value default        | 1000\n"
"| Value recommendation | 10000-100000\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/salt/master.d/tuning.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `pub_hwm: 10000`\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://docs.saltproject.io/en/latest/ref/configuration/master.html#pub-hwm, "
"https://zeromq.org/socket-api/#high-water-mark\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:105
#, no-wrap
msgid "`zmq_backlog`"
msgstr "`zmq_backlog`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:106
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The maximum number of allowed client connections "
"that have started but not concluded the opening process. If more than this "
"number of clients connects in a very short time frame, connections are "
"dropped and clients experience a delay re-connecting.\n"
"| Tune when            | xref:client-count[Client count] increases "
"significantly and very many clients reconnect in a short time frame, TCP "
"connections to the `salt-master` process get dropped by the kernel.\n"
"| Value default        | 1000\n"
"| Value recommendation | 1000-5000\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/salt/master.d/tuning.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `zmq_backlog: 2000`\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://docs.saltproject.io/en/latest/ref/configuration/master.html#zmq-backlog, "
"http://api.zeromq.org/3-0:zmq-getsockopt (`ZMQ_BACKLOG`)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:107
#, no-wrap
msgid "`swappiness`"
msgstr "`swappiness`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:108
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | How aggressively the kernel moves unused data from "
"memory to the swap partition.\n"
"                         Setting a lower parameter typically reduces swap "
"usage and results in better performance, especially when RAM memory is "
"abundant.\n"
"| Tune when            | RAM increases, or swap is used when RAM memory is "
"sufficient.\n"
"| Value default        | 60\n"
"| Value recommendation | 1-60. For 128{nbsp}GB of RAM, 10 is expected to "
"give good results.\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/sysctl.conf``\n"
"| Example              | `vm.swappiness = 20`\n"
"| More information     | "
"{sles-base-os-documentation}/cha-tuning-memory.html#cha-tuning-memory-vm\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:109
#, no-wrap
msgid "`wait_for_backend`"
msgstr "`wait_for_backend`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:110
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | Determines whether the `salt-broker` service should "
"wait for backend sockets to be connected before opening the sockets for "
"listening for connections from `salt-minions`.\n"
"                         When enabled, it helps to prevent collecting ZeroMQ "
"messages with the internal buffers of the sockets and pushing them to the "
"`salt-master` once connection is restored.\n"
"| Tune when            | Unstable connectivity between the {productname} "
"Proxy and the {productname} Server.\n"
"| Value default        | False\n"
"| Value recommendation | True\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/salt/broker``\n"
"| Example              | `wait_for_backend: True`\n"
"| More information     | "
"xref:specialized-guides:salt/salt-connectivity.adoc#proxies-connectivity[Proxies "
"Connectivity]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:111
#, no-wrap
msgid "`tcp_keepalive`"
msgstr "`tcp_keepalive`"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:112
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Description          | The tcp keepalive interval to set on TCP "
"ports. This setting can be used to tune Salt connectivity issues in messy "
"network environments with misbehaving firewalls.\n"
"| Tune when            | Unstable connectivity between managed clients and "
"the {productname} Proxy or the {productname} Server.\n"
"| Value default        | True\n"
"| Value recommendation | True\n"
"| Location             | [path]``/etc/venv-salt-minon/minion.d/tuning.conf`` "
"or [path]``/etc/salt/minion.d/tuning.conf``, depending on the minion type.\n"
"| Example              | `tcp_keepalive: True`\n"
"| After changing       | Check "
"xref:specialized-guides:salt/salt-connectivity.adoc#minions-connectivity[Minions "
"Connectivity] for more details to fine tune extra keepalive parameters.\n"
"| More information     | "
"https://docs.saltproject.io/en/latest/ref/configuration/minion.html#tcp-keepalive, "
"xref:specialized-guides:salt/salt-connectivity.adoc#minions-connectivity[Minions "
"Connectivity]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "Memory Usage"
msgstr "ການນຳໃຊ້ໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:114
msgid ""
"Adjusting some of the parameters listed in this section can result in a "
"higher amount of RAM being used by various components.  It is important that "
"the amount of hardware RAM is adequate after any significant change."
msgstr "ການປັບແຕ່ງບາງພາຣາມິເຕີໃນພາກນີ້ອາດເຮັດໃຫ້ຄອມໂພເນັນຕ່າງໆໃຊ້ RAM ຫຼາຍຂຶ້ນ. ມັນສຳຄັນຫຼາຍທີ່ຕ້ອງໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າຈຳນວນ RAM ຂອງຮາດແວມີພຽງພໍຫຼັງຈາກມີການປ່ຽນແປງທີ່ສຳຄັນ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:115
msgid ""
"To determine how RAM is being used, you will need to check each process that "
"consumes it."
msgstr "ເພື່ອເບິ່ງວ່າ RAM ຖືກໃຊ້ແນວໃດ, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງກວດສອບແຕ່ລະໂປຣເຊສທີ່ນຳໃຊ້ RAM."

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:116
#, no-wrap
msgid "Operating system"
msgstr "ລະບົບປະຕິບັດການ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:117
msgid ""
"Stop all {productname} services and inspect the output of [command]``free "
"-h``."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:118
#, no-wrap
msgid "Java-based components"
msgstr "ຄອມໂພເນັນທີ່ອີງຕາມ Java"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:119
msgid ""
"This includes Taskomatic, Tomcat, and `rhn-search`.  These services support "
"a configurable memory cap."
msgstr "ລວມມີ Taskomatic, Tomcat, ແລະ `rhn-search`. ບໍລິການເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຮອງຮັບການກຳນົດຂີດຈຳກັດໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳ."

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:120
#, no-wrap
msgid "The {productname} Server"
msgstr "{productname} Server"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:121
msgid ""
"Depends on many factors and can only be estimated.  Measure PostgreSQL "
"reserved memory by checking xref:shared-buffers[`shared_buffers`], "
"permanently.  You can also multiply xref:work-mem[`work_mem`] and "
"xref:max-connections[`max_connections`], and multiply by three for a worst "
"case estimate of per-query RAM.  You will also need to check the operating "
"system buffers and caches, which are used by PostgreSQL to host copies of "
"database data.  These often automatically occupy any available RAM."
msgstr "ຂຶ້ນກັບຫຼາຍປັດໄຈ ແລະ ສາມາດປະເມີນໄດ້ເທົ່ານັ້ນ. ໃຫ້ວັດແທກໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳທີ່ PostgreSQL ຈອງໄວ້ໂດຍການກວດສອບ xref:shared-buffers[`shared_buffers`]. ເຈົ້າຍັງສາມາດຄູນ xref:work-mem[`work_mem`] ກັບ xref:max-connections[`max_connections`], ແລະ ຄູນດ້ວຍສາມສຳລັບການປະເມີນໃນກໍລະນີທີ່ແຍ່ທີ່ສຸດຂອງ RAM ຕໍ່ query. ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງກວດສອບ buffers ແລະ caches ຂອງລະບົບປະຕິບັດການນຳອີກ, ເຊິ່ງ PostgreSQL ໃຊ້ເພື່ອເກັບຂໍ້ມູນຖານຂໍ້ມູນ. ສິ່ງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ມັກຈະຈອງ RAM ທີ່ວ່າງຢູ່ທັງໝົດໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:122
msgid ""
"It is important that the {productname} Server has sufficient RAM to "
"accommodate all of these processes, especially OS buffers and caches, to "
"have reasonable PostgreSQL performance.  We recommend you keep several "
"gigabytes available at all times, and add more as the database size on disk "
"increases."
msgstr "ມັນສຳຄັນຫຼາຍທີ່ {productname} Server ຕ້ອງມີ RAM ພຽງພໍສຳລັບທຸກໂປຣເຊສເຫຼົ່ານີ້, ໂດຍສະເພາະ OS buffers ແລະ caches, ເພື່ອໃຫ້ PostgreSQL ມີປະສິດທິພາບທີ່ດີ. ພວກເຮົາແນະນຳໃຫ້ມີ RAM ວ່າງໄວ້ຫຼາຍໆ Gigabyte ຕະຫຼອດເວລາ, ແລະ ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນຕາມຂະໜາດຂອງຖານຂໍ້ມູນໃນດິດ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:123
msgid ""
"Whenever the expected amount of memory available for OS buffers and caches "
"changes, update the `effective_cache_size` parameter to have PostgreSQL use "
"it correctly.  You can calculate the total available by finding the total "
"RAM available, less the expected memory usage."
msgstr "ເມື່ອໃດກໍຕາມທີ່ໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳສຳລັບ OS buffers ແລະ caches ປ່ຽນແປງ, ໃຫ້ອັບເດດພາຣາມິເຕີ `effective_cache_size` ເພື່ອໃຫ້ PostgreSQL ນຳໃຊ້ໄດ້ຢ່າງຖືກຕ້ອງ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດຄຳນວນໄດ້ຈາກ RAM ທັງໝົດ ຫັກອອກດ້ວຍໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳທີ່ຄາດວ່າຈະຖືກນຳໃຊ້."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:124
msgid ""
"To get a live breakdown of the memory used by services on the {productname} "
"Server, use this command:"
msgstr "ເພື່ອເບິ່ງລາຍລະອຽດການໃຊ້ໜ່ວຍຄວາມຈຳຂອງບໍລິການຕ່າງໆໃນ {productname} Server ແບບສົດໆ, ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ຄຳສັ່ງນີ້:"

#. type: delimited block -
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:125
#, no-wrap
msgid "pidstat -p ALL -r --human 1 60 | tee pidstat-memory.log\n"
msgstr "pidstat -p ALL -r --human 1 60 | tee pidstat-memory.log\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/large-deployments/tuning.adoc:126
msgid ""
"This command will save a copy of displayed data in the `pidstat-memory.log` "
"file for later analysis."
msgstr "ຄຳສັ່ງນີ້ຈະບັນທຶກສຳເນົາຂໍ້ມູນທີ່ສະແດງໃນໄຟລ໌ `pidstat-memory.log` ເພື່ອໄວ້ວິເຄາະພາຍຫຼັງ."

#. type: Title =
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/byos-overview.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "{byos} Guide"
msgstr "ຄູ່ມື {byos}"

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/byos-overview.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "{byoslongform} ({byos})"
msgstr "{byoslongform} ({byos})"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/byos-overview.adoc:3
msgid ""
"{byoslongform} ({byos}) images are useful if you already have a support "
"contract with SUSE and want to move your workloads to the public cloud.  An "
"instance launched from a {byos} image is equivalent to a physical machine "
"that just received a SUSE Linux Enterprise Server installation from the "
"{sles} installation image."
msgstr "ອິເມຈ {byoslongform} ({byos}) ແມ່ນມີປະໂຫຍດຫາກເຈົ້າມີສັນຍາການສະໜັບສະໜູນກັບ SUSE ຢູ່ແລ້ວ ແລະ ຕ້ອງການຍ້າຍວຽກໄປຍັງ public cloud. instance ທີ່ເປີດໃຊ້ຈາກອິເມຈ {byos} ຈະເທົ່າກັບເຄື່ອງຈິງທີ່ຫາກໍຕິດຕັ້ງ SUSE Linux Enterprise Server ຈາກອິເມຈຕິດຕັ້ງ {sles}."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/byos-overview.adoc:4
msgid "After creation:"
msgstr "ຫຼັງຈາກສ້າງແລ້ວ:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/byos-overview.adoc:5
msgid ""
"use ``registercloudguest`` to register the instance with the SUSE-operated "
"update infrastructure in the cloud framework, or"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/byos-overview.adoc:6
msgid ""
"use the command ``SUSEConnect`` to register the system with {scclongform} "
"using the entitlements you already have."
msgstr ""

#. type: Block title
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/byos-overview.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid "Obtaining a SUSE Manager Server Subscription for {byos}"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/byos-overview.adoc:8
msgid ""
"To obtain a SUSE Manager Server Lifecycle subscription, customers must send "
"an email to susemanagerkey@suse.com, including proof of running at least 10 "
"instances of SLES for SAP BYOS.  Proof can be a screenshot of the relevant "
"section of the cloud console.  The subscription key is valid for one year, "
"and customers can renew it by providing updated proof of their instances at "
"the end of the period."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/byos-overview.adoc:9
msgid ""
"Connect your system to your own running RMT or {productname} infrastructure "
"in the same way you connect systems in your data center."
msgstr "ເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ລະບົບຂອງເຈົ້າກັບໂຄງລ່າງພື້ນຖານ RMT ຫຼື {productname} ຂອງເຈົ້າເອງ ໃນຮູບແບບດຽວກັນກັບທີ່ເຈົ້າເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ລະບົບໃນ data center."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/byos-overview.adoc:10
msgid ""
"{byos} instances make it easier to manage extensions such as ``LTSS`` or "
"``kernel live-patching``.  Extensions for {payg} instances can only be used "
"in conjunction with {productname}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/clients.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Client Registration"
msgstr "ການລົງທະບຽນໄຄລແອນ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/clients.adoc:2
msgid ""
"When you have your {productname} Server and, optionally, your {productname} "
"Proxy set up, you are ready to start registering clients."
msgstr "ເມື່ອເຈົ້າຕັ້ງຄ່າ {productname} Server ແລະ {productname} Proxy (ຫາກມີ) ແລ້ວ, ເຈົ້າກໍພ້ອມທີ່ຈະເລີ່ມລົງທະບຽນໄຄລແອນ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/clients.adoc:3
msgid ""
"For instructions on registering clients on a public cloud, see "
"xref:client-configuration:clients-pubcloud.adoc[]."
msgstr "ສຳລັບຄຳແນະນຳໃນການລົງທະບຽນໄຄລແອນໃນ public cloud, ເບິ່ງ xref:client-configuration:clients-pubcloud.adoc[]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/clients.adoc:4
msgid ""
"For instructions on connecting {payg} instances, see "
"xref:installation-and-upgrade:connect-payg.adoc[]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/clients.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additional Resources"
msgstr "ຊັບພະຍາກອນເພີ່ມເຕີມ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/clients.adoc:6
msgid ""
"For more information on using {suse} products in the public cloud see: "
"link:https://documentation.suse.com/sle-public-cloud/all/html/public-cloud/cha-intro.html[SUSE "
"Linux Enterprise Public Cloud Guide]."
msgstr "ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການໃຊ້ຜະລິດຕະພັນ {suse} ໃນ public cloud ເບິ່ງ: link:https://documentation.suse.com/sle-public-cloud/all/html/public-cloud/cha-intro.html[SUSE Linux Enterprise Public Cloud Guide]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/clients.adoc:7
msgid ""
"For more {productname} product documentation, see "
"https://documentation.suse.com/suma."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/clients.adoc:8
msgid ""
"To raise an issue or propose a change to the documentation, use the links "
"under the ``Resources`` menu on the documentation site."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title =
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:1
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/payg/azure/payg-azure-server-setup.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initial Setup"
msgstr "ການຕັ້ງຄ່າເບື້ອງຕົ້ນ"

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:2
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/public-cloud-faq.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "ບົດນຳ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:3
msgid ""
"This guide shows you the fastest way to get {productname} up and running in "
"a public cloud using on-demand or {byos} services.  We have tested using "
"{productname} on Amazon EC2, Google Compute Engine, and Microsoft Azure, but "
"these procedures should work with other public cloud providers as well, with "
"some variation."
msgstr "ຄູ່ມືນີ້ຈະສະແດງວິທີທີ່ໄວທີ່ສຸດໃນການຕິດຕັ້ງ {productname} ໃຫ້ພ້ອມໃຊ້ງານໃນ public cloud ໂດຍໃຊ້ບໍລິການແບບ on-demand ຫຼື {byos}. ພວກເຮົາໄດ້ທົດສອບການໃຊ້ {productname} ໃນ Amazon EC2, Google Compute Engine, ແລະ Microsoft Azure ແລ້ວ, ແຕ່ຂັ້ນຕອນເຫຼົ່ານີ້ກໍສາມາດໃຊ້ກັບຜູ້ໃຫ້ບໍລິການ public cloud ອື່ນໆໄດ້ເຊັ່ນກັນ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:4
msgid ""
"There are three main methods of using {productname} on a public cloud "
"service."
msgstr "ມີສາມວິທີຫຼັກໃນການໃຊ້ {productname} ໃນບໍລິການ public cloud."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:5
msgid ""
"{byoslongform} ({byos}):: Most public cloud providers make a {byos} image of "
"{productname} available.  This means you do not need to install "
"{productname}, just set up the server or proxy.  You will need to have "
"{suse} product entitlements before you begin, and there are some additional "
"setup steps required.  The public cloud documentation in the {productname} "
"documentation suite assumes you are using this method."
msgstr "{byoslongform} ({byos}):: ຜູ້ໃຫ້ບໍລິການ public cloud ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ຈະມີອິເມຈ {byos} ຂອງ {productname} ໃຫ້ບໍລິການ. ສິ່ງນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າເຈົ້າບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຕິດຕັ້ງ {productname}, ພຽງແຕ່ຕັ້ງຄ່າ server ຫຼື proxy ກໍພໍ. ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງມີສິດການນຳໃຊ້ຜະລິດຕະພັນ {suse} ກ່ອນເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ແລະ ຈະມີບາງຂັ້ນຕອນການຕັ້ງຄ່າເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Virtual machine on public cloud"
msgstr "Virtual machine ໃນ public cloud"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:7
msgid ""
"In this method, you subscribe to a public cloud service, and install "
"{productname} in a virtual machine, using the {unifiedinstaller}.  You will "
"need to have {suse} product entitlements before you begin.  You can do this "
"by following all the same instructions as you would for any local "
"{productname} installation."
msgstr "ໃນວິທີນີ້, ເຈົ້າສະໝັກໃຊ້ບໍລິການ public cloud ແລະ ຕິດຕັ້ງ {productname} ໃນ virtual machine ໂດຍໃຊ້ {unifiedinstaller}. ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງມີສິດການນຳໃຊ້ຜະລິດຕະພັນ {suse} ກ່ອນເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ. ເຈົ້າສາມາດເຮັດຕາມຂັ້ນຕອນດຽວກັນກັບການຕິດຕັ້ງ {productname} ແບບທົ່ວໄປ."

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid "On-demand {sles} {payglongform} ({payg}) image"
msgstr "ອິເມຈ On-demand {sles} {payglongform} ({payg})"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:9
msgid ""
"Most public cloud providers make {sles} available as a {byos} image.  This "
"means that {sles} is pre-installed, and you can install {productname} on "
"top, using the {unifiedinstaller}.  You can do this by following all the "
"same instructions as you would for any local {productname} installation.  "
"You will need to have {suse} product entitlements before you begin.  Be "
"careful with this method, because you might end up requiring additional "
"product entitlements that could drive up your costs."
msgstr "ຜູ້ໃຫ້ບໍລິການ public cloud ສ່ວນໃຫຍ່ມີ {sles} ໃນຮູບແບບອິເມຈ {byos}. ສິ່ງນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າ {sles} ຖືກຕິດຕັ້ງໄວ້ແລ້ວ, ແລະ ເຈົ້າສາມາດຕິດຕັ້ງ {productname} ເພີ່ມເຕີມໄດ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ {unifiedinstaller}. ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງມີສິດການນຳໃຊ້ຜະລິດຕະພັນ {suse} ກ່ອນເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ. ໃຫ້ລະວັງວິທີນີ້ ເພາະເຈົ້າອາດຕ້ອງໃຊ້ສິດການນຳໃຊ້ຜະລິດຕະພັນເພີ່ມເຕີມເຊິ່ງອາດເຮັດໃຫ້ຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍສູງຂຶ້ນ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "{productname} Server"
msgstr "{productname} Server"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:11
msgid ""
"If you are using the {byos} method, start by logging in to your chosen "
"public cloud provider, and launching a {productname} instance.  Depending on "
"the public cloud you are using, you can usually locate the {productname} "
"Server {byos} images by searching for ``suse manager``.  In EC2, you need to "
"search within the Community AMIs.  In GCE and Azure, search the marketplace."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:12
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:16
msgid ""
"Select a public cloud instance type that meets the hardware and networking "
"requirements in xref:installation-and-upgrade:pubcloud-requirements.adoc[]."
msgstr "ເລືອກປະເພດ instance ໃນ public cloud ທີ່ຕອບສະໜອງຄວາມຕ້ອງການດ້ານຮາດແວ ແລະ ເຄືອຂ່າຍໃນ xref:installation-and-upgrade:pubcloud-requirements.adoc[]."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:13
msgid ""
"When you have your virtual machine ready, and the {byos} image installed, "
"you need to set up {productname} Server.  This is done in the same way as a "
"local installation, using {yast}.  When you have completed {productname} "
"setup, you need to activate the public cloud module.  You can then complete "
"the setup in the {productname} {webui}."
msgstr "ເມື່ອ virtual machine ພ້ອມແລ້ວ ແລະ ຕິດຕັ້ງອິເມຈ {byos} ແລ້ວ, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງຕັ້ງຄ່າ {productname} Server. ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດໄດ້ໃນຮູບແບບດຽວກັນກັບການຕິດຕັ້ງແບບທົ່ວໄປໂດຍໃຊ້ {yast}. ເມື່ອສຳເລັດການຕັ້ງຄ່າ, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງເປີດໃຊ້ public cloud module, ແລ້ວຈຶ່ງໄປຕັ້ງຄ່າໃຫ້ສຳເລັດໃນ {productname} {webui}."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid "{productname} Proxy"
msgstr "{productname} Proxy"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:15
msgid ""
"You must use the {byos} method.  Start by logging in to your chosen public "
"cloud provider, and launch a {productname} Proxy instance.  Depending on the "
"public cloud you are using, you can usually locate the {productname} Proxy "
"{byos} images by searching for ``suse manager proxy``.  In EC2, you need to "
"search within the Community AMIs.  In GCE and Azure, search the marketplace."
msgstr ""

#.  You can then complete setup in the {productname} {webui}.
#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/byos/setup.adoc:17
msgid ""
"When you have your virtual machine ready, and the {byos} image installed, "
"you need to set up {productname} Proxy.  This is done in the same way as a "
"local installation, using {suse} setup tools.  When you have completed "
"{productname} Proxy setup, you need to activate the public cloud module."
msgstr "ເມື່ອ virtual machine ພ້ອມແລ້ວ ແລະ ຕິດຕັ້ງອິເມຈ {byos} ແລ້ວ, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງຕັ້ງຄ່າ {productname} Proxy. ສິ່ງນີ້ເຮັດໄດ້ໃນຮູບແບບດຽວກັນກັບການຕິດຕັ້ງແບບທົ່ວໄປໂດຍໃຊ້ເຄື່ອງມືຂອງ {suse}. ເມື່ອສຳເລັດການຕັ້ງຄ່າ, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງເປີດໃຊ້ public cloud module."

#. type: Title =
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-appendix.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix"
msgstr "ເອກະສານຊ້ອນທ້າຍ"

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-appendix.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Countries that can transact {productname} {payg} through the cloud "
"marketplace"
msgstr "ປະເທດທີ່ສາມາດຊື້-ຂາຍ {productname} {payg} ຜ່ານ cloud marketplace ໄດ້"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-appendix.adoc:3
msgid ""
"Countries that can transact via the cloud marketplaces: "
"link:https://documentation.suse.com/sle-public-cloud/all/html/public-cloud/countrylist.html#[Supported "
"Country List]"
msgstr "ປະເທດທີ່ສາມາດຊື້-ຂາຍຜ່ານ cloud marketplaces: link:https://documentation.suse.com/sle-public-cloud/all/html/public-cloud/countrylist.html#[ລາຍຊື່ປະເທດທີ່ຮອງຮັບ]"

#. type: Title =
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Billing - General"
msgstr "ການຄິດໄລ່ຄ່າບໍລິການ - ທົ່ວໄປ"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:2
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:2
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:2
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/public-cloud-faq.adoc:2
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/troubleshooting/tshoot-public-cloud-intro.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Last updated:** {lastupdate}\n"
msgstr "**ອັບເດດຫຼ້າສຸດ:** {lastupdate}\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I have an existing {productname} {byos} subscription; can I use this on the "
"cloud?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍມີການສະໝັກໃຊ້ {productname} {byos} ຢູ່ແລ້ວ; ຂ້ອຍສາມາດໃຊ້ມັນໃນ cloud ໄດ້ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:4
msgid ""
"{byos} {byoslongform} {productname} deployments are supported on the cloud, "
"however, billing will not be via the cloud marketplace."
msgstr "ການວາງລະບົບ {byos} {byoslongform} {productname} ແມ່ນຮອງຮັບໃນ cloud, ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ການເກັບເງິນຈະບໍ່ຜ່ານ cloud marketplace."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Once the existing subscription term ends, you can purchase {productname} "
"{payg} via the cloud provider marketplace and manage your instances with a "
"{productname} deployment that is billed via the cloud."
msgstr "ເມື່ອໄລຍະເວລາການສະໝັກໃຊ້ທີ່ມີຢູ່ສິ້ນສຸດລົງ, ເຈົ້າສາມາດຊື້ {productname} {payg} ຜ່ານ cloud marketplace ແລະ ຈັດການ instance ຂອງເຈົ້າດ້ວຍ {productname} ທີ່ເກັບເງິນຜ່ານ cloud ໄດ້."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I have an existing deployment covered by a {byos} {productname} "
"subscription; can I use this new listing in the cloud for a separate "
"deployment of {productname} {payg}?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍມີການວາງລະບົບທີ່ຄຸ້ມຄອງໂດຍ {byos} {productname} ຢູ່ແລ້ວ; ຂ້ອຍສາມາດໃຊ້ລາຍການໃໝ່ນີ້ໃນ cloud ສຳລັບການວາງລະບົບ {productname} {payg} ແຍກຕ່າງຫາກໄດ້ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:7
msgid ""
"Yes, the listing works independently from your existing {byos} {productname} "
"subscriptions. Please remember that support processes may be different for "
"deployments using your existing {byos} subscription and those billed via the "
"cloud and note that there is currently no process for migrating deployments "
"between {byos} and {payg} versions."
msgstr "ໄດ້, ລາຍການນີ້ເຮັດວຽກແຍກຕ່າງຫາກຈາກການສະໝັກໃຊ້ {byos} {productname} ທີ່ມີຢູ່. ກະລຸນາຈື່ໄວ້ວ່າຂະບວນການສະໜັບສະໜູນອາດຈະຕ່າງກັນ ແລະ ໃນປະຈຸບັນຍັງບໍ່ມີຂະບວນການຍ້າຍລະບົບລະຫວ່າງເວີຊັນ {byos} ແລະ {payg}."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:8
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Tell me more about how the billing for {productname} {payg} works via the "
"cloud?"
msgstr "ຊ່ວຍອະທິບາຍເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບວິທີການຄິດໄລ່ຄ່າບໍລິການ {productname} {payg} ຜ່ານ cloud ໄດ້ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:9
msgid ""
"When purchasing {productname} via the {availability} Marketplaces, the "
"billing is as follows:"
msgstr "ເມື່ອຊື້ {productname} ຜ່ານ {availability} Marketplaces, ການເກັບເງິນຈະເປັນດັ່ງນີ້:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:10
msgid "Billing is monthly and handled via cloud marketplace."
msgstr "ການເກັບເງິນແມ່ນເປັນລາຍເດືອນ ແລະ ຈັດການຜ່ານ cloud marketplace."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:11
msgid "Managed instances are recorded hourly."
msgstr "Instance ທີ່ຖືກຈັດການຈະຖືກບັນທຶກທຸກໆຊົ່ວໂມງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:12
msgid "The peak usage total is recorded for the month."
msgstr "ຈຳນວນການໃຊ້ງານສູງສຸດຈະຖືກບັນທຶກໄວ້ໃນແຕ່ລະເດືອນ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:13
msgid "There is a monthly usage charge for each instance in the count."
msgstr "ມີຄ່າບໍລິການລາຍເດືອນສຳລັບແຕ່ລະ instance ທີ່ຢູ່ໃນການຄິດໄລ່."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:14
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I have existing SLES for SAP instances procured via the cloud provider "
"marketplace, is there a cost to manage these instance with {productname} "
"{payg}?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍມີ SLES for SAP instances ທີ່ຊື້ຜ່ານ cloud marketplace ຢູ່ແລ້ວ, ຈະມີຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍໃນການຈັດການ instance ເຫຼົ່ານີ້ດ້ວຍ {productname} {payg} ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:15
msgid ""
"SLES for SAP Applications {payg}/on-demand instances, when purchased via the "
"cloud marketplace, include Lifecycle Management(LCM) entitlements for "
"{productname}."
msgstr "instance SLES for SAP Applications ແບບ {payg}/on-demand ເມື່ອຊື້ຜ່ານ cloud marketplace ຈະລວມມີສິດການນຳໃຊ້ Lifecycle Management (LCM) ສຳລັບ {productname} ຢູ່ແລ້ວ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:16
msgid ""
"The {productname} {payg} billing engine recognizes the embedded LCM "
"entitlements and does not include them in the count. This means there are no "
"additional charges to manage these with the {productname} {payg} listing."
msgstr "ລະບົບການເກັບເງິນຂອງ {productname} {payg} ຈະຮັບຮູ້ສິດ LCM ທີ່ຕິດມານັ້ນ ແລະ ຈະບໍ່ລວມພວກມັນເຂົ້າໃນການຄິດໄລ່. ສິ່ງນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າບໍ່ມີຄ່າບໍລິການເພີ່ມເຕີມໃນການຈັດການພວກມັນ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:17
msgid ""
"However, if {productname} Monitoring is required for these instances, "
"additional charges will apply for this feature."
msgstr "ແນວໃດກໍຕາມ, ຫາກຕ້ອງການໃຊ້ {productname} Monitoring ສຳລັບ instance ເຫຼົ່ານີ້, ຈະມີຄ່າບໍລິການເພີ່ມເຕີມສຳລັບຟີເຈີນີ້ນ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "Is there a way to try {productname} {payg} before purchasing?"
msgstr "ມີວິທີທົດລອງໃຊ້ {productname} {payg} ກ່ອນຊື້ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:19
msgid ""
"If using the {productname} {payg} listing in the cloud marketplace, billing "
"will commence from the time of deployment and when applicable client "
"instances are on-boarded to {productname}."
msgstr "ຫາກໃຊ້ລາຍການ {productname} {payg} ໃນ cloud marketplace, ການເກັບເງິນຈະເລີ່ມຕັ້ງແຕ່ຕອນວາງລະບົບ ແລະ ເມື່ອມີການຮັບໄຄລແອນເຂົ້າໃນ {productname}."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:20
msgid ""
"There is the {productname} {byos} listing in the cloud marketplace that can "
"be used, a trial subscription key can be obtained via the SUSE Website. This "
"deployment cannot be directly converted to allow billing via cloud "
"marketplaces."
msgstr "ເຈົ້າສາມາດໃຊ້ລາຍການ {productname} {byos} ໃນ cloud marketplace ໄດ້, ໂດຍສາມາດຂໍລະຫັດທົດລອງໃຊ້ໄດ້ຈາກເວັບໄຊ SUSE. ແຕ່ການວາງລະບົບນີ້ບໍ່ສາມາດປ່ຽນເປັນແບບເກັບເງິນຜ່ານ cloud marketplace ໂດຍກົງໄດ້."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:21
msgid ""
"To benefit from monthly billing via the cloud marketplace, {productname} "
"needs to be redeployed using the version from the {payg} listing in the "
"cloud marketplace."
msgstr "ເພື່ອໃຫ້ສາມາດເກັບເງິນລາຍເດືອນຜ່ານ cloud marketplace, {productname} ຈະຕ້ອງຖືກຕິດຕັ້ງໃໝ່ໂດຍໃຊ້ເວີຊັນຈາກລາຍການ {payg} ໃນ cloud marketplace."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:22
#, no-wrap
msgid "How does SUSE calculate the amount of managed instances to bill for?"
msgstr "SUSE ຄຳນວນຈຳນວນ instance ທີ່ຖືກຈັດການເພື່ອເກັບເງິນແນວໃດ?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:23
msgid "Billing is based on the number of managed instances."
msgstr "ການເກັບເງິນແມ່ນອີງຕາມຈຳນວນ instance ທີ່ຖືກຈັດການ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:24
msgid ""
"Below are 3 examples of how the node count is calculated, check the table "
"below for the detail."
msgstr "ດ້ານລຸ່ມນີ້ແມ່ນ 3 ຕົວຢ່າງຂອງການຄຳນວນຈຳນວນ node, ໃຫ້ເບິ່ງລາຍລະອຽດໃນຕາຕະລາງ."

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "Static usage"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ງານແບບຄົງທີ່"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:26
msgid ""
"Using {productname} with 10 instances registered for management, for 1 month "
"with no additional managed clients added in the month."
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ {productname} ກັບ 10 instances ທີ່ລົງທະບຽນຈັດການ ເປັນເວລາ 1 ເດືອນ ໂດຍບໍ່ມີການເພີ່ມໄຄລແອນໃໝ່."

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bursting Model"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ງານແບບມີການເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນຊົ່ວຄາວ (Bursting Model)"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:28
msgid ""
"Using {productname} with 10 instances registered for management for 3 weeks "
"in the month, bursting to 30 managed instances for 1 week."
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ {productname} ກັບ 10 instances ເປັນເວລາ 3 ອາທິດໃນໜຶ່ງເດືອນ, ແລະ ເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນເປັນ 30 instances ເປັນເວລາ 1 ອາທິດ."

#. type: Labeled list
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transient model"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ງານແບບຊົ່ວຄາວ (Transient model)"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:30
msgid ""
"A temporary deployment of {productname} with 20 managed instances, for 2 "
"weeks (336 hours)"
msgstr "ການວາງລະບົບ {productname} ຊົ່ວຄາວທີ່ມີ 20 instances, ເປັນເວລາ 2 ອາທິດ (336 ຊົ່ວໂມງ)"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:31
msgid ""
"The total is calculated by counting number of active nodes (checked "
"hourly).  There is a monthly charge for each managed node under management "
"in the billing cycle."
msgstr "ຍອດລວມຈະຖືກຄຳນວນໂດຍການນັບຈຳນວນ node ທີ່ເຮັດວຽກຢູ່ (ກວດສອບທຸກຊົ່ວໂມງ). ມີຄ່າບໍລິການລາຍເດືອນສຳລັບແຕ່ລະ node ທີ່ຢູ່ພາຍໃຕ້ການຈັດການໃນຮອບການເກັບເງິນ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:32
msgid "Below are 3 examples of how the average node count is calculated."
msgstr "ດ້ານລຸ່ມນີ້ແມ່ນ 3 ຕົວຢ່າງຂອງການຄຳນວນຈຳນວນ node ສະເລ່ຍ."

#. type: Block title
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid "Usage calculations for different scenarios"
msgstr "ການຄຳນວນການໃຊ້ງານສຳລັບສະຖານະການຕ່າງໆ"

#. type: Table
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|  |Managed Instances |Peak Usage |Billed for\n"
"|Static Usage |10 |10 |10\n"
"|Bursting Model |10 - 3 Weeks, 30 - 1 Week|30 |30\n"
"|Transient Cluster |20 - 2 Weeks |20 |20\n"
msgstr ""
"|  |Managed Instances |Peak Usage |Billed for\n"
"|ການໃຊ້ງານແບບຄົງທີ່ |10 |10 |10\n"
"|ການໃຊ້ງານແບບມີການເພີ່ມຂຶ້ນຊົ່ວຄາວ |10 - 3 ອາທິດ, 30 - 1 ອາທິດ|30 |30\n"
"|ຄລັສເຕີຊົ່ວຄາວ |20 - 2 ອາທິດ |20 |20\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "Are special commercial terms available?"
msgstr "ມີເງື່ອນໄຂທາງການຄ້າພິເສດບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:36
msgid ""
"It is dependent on the deployment and the cloud provider, as every Cloud "
"Service Provider (CSP) has its own commercial terms and offers."
msgstr "ສິ່ງນີ້ຂຶ້ນກັບການວາງລະບົບ ແລະ ຜູ້ໃຫ້ບໍລິການ cloud, ເນື່ອງຈາກແຕ່ລະ CSP ມີເງື່ອນໄຂ ແລະ ຂໍ້ສະເໜີທາງການຄ້າຂອງຕົນເອງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:37
msgid ""
"It may be possible to secure special commercial terms such as an annual "
"subscription. For example, AWS can offer {productname} {payg} via a Private "
"Offer. Please contact SUSE for more information."
msgstr "ອາດຈະມີການກຳນົດເງື່ອນໄຂພິເສດ ເຊັ່ນ ການສະໝັກໃຊ້ລາຍປີ. ຕົວຢ່າງ: AWS ສາມາດສະເໜີ {productname} {payg} ຜ່ານ Private Offer ໄດ້. ກະລຸນາຕິດຕໍ່ SUSE ສຳລັບຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Can my spending on {productname} {payg} count towards my committed spend "
"with the cloud provider?"
msgstr "ຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍໃນ {productname} {payg} ສາມາດນັບລວມເຂົ້າໃນຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍທີ່ຜູກພັນ (committed spend) ກັບຜູ້ໃຫ້ບໍລິການ cloud ໄດ້ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:39
msgid "There are such programs at the cloud providers:"
msgstr "ມີໂປຣແກຣມດັ່ງກ່າວຢູ່ທີ່ຜູ້ໃຫ້ບໍລິການ cloud:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:40
msgid "Azure MACC Program"
msgstr "Azure MACC Program"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:41
msgid "AWS Enterprise Discount Program"
msgstr "AWS Enterprise Discount Program"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:42
msgid "Google CUD"
msgstr "Google CUD"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:43
msgid "Yes, it can. Please contact your cloud provider sales team for more details."
msgstr "ໄດ້, ກະລຸນາຕິດຕໍ່ທີມງານຂາຍຂອງຜູ້ໃຫ້ບໍລິການ cloud ຂອງເຈົ້າສຳລັບລາຍລະອຽດເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:44
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How do I purchase {productname} / LCM subscriptions for additional managed "
"instances?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍຈະຊື້ການສະໝັກໃຊ້ {productname} / LCM ສຳລັບ instance ເພີ່ມເຕີມໄດ້ແນວໃດ?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:45
msgid ""
"Once {productname} {payg} has been deployed from the marketplace listing and "
"billing is active, there is no need to make a specific purchase to manage "
"additional instances. Billing is dynamic and based on the number of "
"instances {productname} is managing. Just on-board additional instances to "
"{productname} as needed, this will be reflected in your cloud marketplace "
"bill."
msgstr "ເມື່ອວາງລະບົບ {productname} {payg} ຈາກ marketplace ແລ້ວ, ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງທຳການຊື້ແຍກຕ່າງຫາກສຳລັບ instance ເພີ່ມເຕີມ. ການເກັບເງິນຈະເປັນແບບ dynamic ຕາມຈຳນວນ instance ທີ່ຈັດການຢູ່. ພຽງແຕ່ຮັບ instance ເຂົ້າໃນລະບົບຕາມທີ່ຕ້ອງການ, ຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍຈະປາກົດໃນໃບບິນ cloud marketplace ຂອງເຈົ້າເອງ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "Is this an annual commitment, will it auto-renew?"
msgstr "ສິ່ງນີ້ເປັນຂໍ້ຜູກພັນລາຍປີບໍ່, ແລະ ຈະຕໍ່ອາຍຸອັດຕະໂນມັດບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:47
msgid ""
"By default, the {productname} {payg} listing on the cloud is billed on a "
"monthly cycle, based on usage. Billing is ongoing for as long as "
"{productname} is deployed and instances are registered."
msgstr "ໂດຍເລີ່ມຕົ້ນ, ລາຍການ {productname} {payg} ໃນ cloud ຈະຖືກເກັບເງິນເປັນຮອບລາຍເດືອນຕາມການໃຊ້ງານ. ການເກັບເງິນຈະດຳເນີນໄປເລື້ອຍໆ ຕາບໃດທີ່ມີການວາງລະບົບ {productname} ແລະ ມີ instance ທີ່ລົງທະບຽນຢູ່."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "Is there a volume discount / tiered pricing built into the Cloud Listing?"
msgstr "ມີສ່ວນຫຼຸດຕາມປະລິມານ (volume discount) ຫຼື ລາຄາແບບຂັ້ນໄດ (tiered pricing) ໃນ Cloud Listing ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:49
msgid "Currently, there is no volume discount available."
msgstr "ໃນປະຈຸບັນ, ຍັງບໍ່ມີສ່ວນຫຼຸດຕາມປະລິມານ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:50
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I no longer require support; how can I end the {productname} {payg} "
"subscription?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍບໍ່ຕ້ອງການການສະໜັບສະໜູນແລ້ວ; ຂ້ອຍຈະສິ້ນສຸດການສະໝັກໃຊ້ {productname} {payg} ໄດ້ແນວໃດ?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:51
msgid "If you no longer require support, there are 2 options:"
msgstr "ຫາກເຈົ້າບໍ່ຕ້ອງການການສະໜັບສະໜູນແລ້ວ, ມີ 2 ທາງເລືອກ:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:52
msgid "Unregister all systems from the {productname} Server"
msgstr "ຍົກເລີກການລົງທະບຽນທຸກລະບົບອອກຈາກ {productname} Server"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-general.adoc:53
msgid "Terminate the {productname} instance."
msgstr "ຢຸດການເຮັດວຽກ (Terminate) ຂອງ {productname} instance."

#. type: Title =
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Billing - Products"
msgstr "ການຄິດໄລ່ຄ່າບໍລິການ - ຜະລິດຕະພັນ"

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How do I migrate an existing {productname} {byos} instance to the {payg} - "
"{payglongform} version?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍຈະຍ້າຍອິນສະແຕນຊ໌ {productname} {byos} ທີ່ມີຢູ່ແລ້ວໄປເປັນເວີຊັນ {payg} - {payglongform} ໄດ້ແນວໃດ?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:3
msgid ""
"Currently, it is *not possible* to migrate an existing instance to the "
"{payg} version."
msgstr "ໃນປະຈຸບັນ, *ຍັງບໍ່ສາມາດ* ຍ້າຍ instance ທີ່ມີຢູ່ໄປເປັນເວີຊັນ {payg} ໄດ້."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:4
msgid ""
"Customers can simply deploy a new {productname} {payg} instance from the "
"cloud marketplace and re-onboard all instances using the standard process."
msgstr "ລູກຄ້າສາມາດວາງລະບົບ {productname} {payg} ໃໝ່ຈາກ cloud marketplace ແລະ ຮັບ instance ທັງໝົດເຂົ້າລະບົບໃໝ່ໂດຍໃຊ້ຂະບວນການມາດຕະຖານ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:5
msgid ""
"link:https://documentation.suse.com/suma/4.3/en/suse-manager/client-configuration/client-config-overview.html[Client "
"configuration overview]"
msgstr "link:https://documentation.suse.com/suma/4.3/en/suse-manager/client-configuration/client-config-overview.html[ພາບລວມການກຳນົດຄ່າໄຄລແອນ]"

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "How do I get support?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍຈະຂໍຮັບການສະໜັບສະໜູນໄດ້ແນວໃດ?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:7
msgid "It is simple to open a support case with SUSE for {productname} {payg}."
msgstr "ການເປີດ support case ກັບ SUSE ສຳລັບ {productname} {payg} ແມ່ນເຮັດໄດ້ງ່າຍໆ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:8
msgid ""
"Create a ‘supportconfig’ via {productname} {payg} instance CLI and upload "
"the output to the {scclongform} ({scc}) at the following link:"
msgstr "ສ້າງ ‘supportconfig’ ຜ່ານ CLI ຂອງ {productname} {payg} instance ແລະ ອັບໂຫຼດຜົນລັອກໄປຍັງ {scclongform} ({scc}) ຕາມລິ້ງນີ້:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:9
msgid "https://scc.suse.com/cloudsupport"
msgstr "https://scc.suse.com/cloudsupport"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:10
msgid "Providing marketplace billing is active, a support case will be opened."
msgstr "ຫາກການເກັບເງິນຜ່ານ marketplace ຍັງເຮັດວຽກຢູ່, support case ຈະຖືກເປີດໃຫ້."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Are there any differences between the {productname} {payg} product on the "
"cloud marketplaces compared to the versions I can run in my own data center?"
msgstr "ຜະລິດຕະພັນ {productname} {payg} ໃນ cloud marketplace ຕ່າງຈາກເວີຊັນທີ່ຂ້ອຍໃຊ້ໃນ data center ຂອງຂ້ອຍເອງບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:12
msgid ""
"The {productname} {payg} product available in the cloud marketplace is the "
"same product, with similar functionality that you would run on-premises or "
"with a manual installation."
msgstr "ຜະລິດຕະພັນ {productname} {payg} ໃນ cloud marketplace ແມ່ນຜະລິດຕະພັນດຽວກັນ, ເຊິ່ງມີຟັງຊັນການເຮັດວຽກຄືກັບເວີຊັນ on-premises ຫຼື ການຕິດຕັ້ງດ້ວຍຕົນເອງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:13
msgid ""
"The only exceptions being the ability to bill via the cloud marketplace and "
"connect to the SUSE Update Infrastructure for {productname} product updates."
msgstr "ຂໍ້ຍົກເວັ້ນພຽງຢ່າງດຽວແມ່ນຄວາມສາມາດໃນການຮຽກເກັບເງິນຜ່ານຕະຫຼາດຄລາວ ແລະ ການເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ກັບໂຄງລ່າງພື້ນຖານການອັບເດດຂອງ SUSE ສໍາລັບການອັບເດດຜະລິດຕະພັນ {productname}."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:14
msgid ""
"It is also worth checking the list of supported client operating systems to "
"ensure your needs are met."
msgstr "ຄວນກວດສອບລາຍຊື່ລະບົບປະຕິບັດການໄຄລແອນທີ່ຮອງຮັບເພື່ອໃຫ້ໝັ້ນໃຈວ່າກົງກັບຄວາມຕ້ອງການຂອງເຈົ້າ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Does the {productname} {payg} instance need to run 24/7?"
msgstr "{productname} {payg} instance ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງເປີດຕະຫຼອດ 24 ຊົ່ວໂມງບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:16
msgid "It is recommended that the {productname} instance always remains active."
msgstr "ແນະນຳໃຫ້ instance ຂອງ {productname} ເປີດເຮັດວຽກຢູ່ຕະຫຼອດເວລາ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How do I get fixes and updates for {productname} {payg}? Do I need a "
"subscription key?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍຈະຮັບການແກ້ໄຂ ແລະ ອັບເດດສຳລັບ {productname} {payg} ໄດ້ແນວໃດ? ຂ້ອຍຕ້ອງມີ subscription key ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:18
msgid ""
"{productname} {payg}, when deployed via the cloud marketplace will "
"automatically connect to the SUSE Update Infrastructure, no separate "
"{productname} subscription key is required."
msgstr "{productname} {payg} ເມື່ອວາງລະບົບຜ່ານ cloud marketplace ຈະເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ກັບ SUSE Update Infrastructure ໂດຍອັດຕະໂນມັດ, ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງໃຊ້ subscription key ແຍກຕ່າງຫາກ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:19
msgid ""
"Updates to the {productname} instance can be applied from those channels "
"using standard SUSE tooling (i.e. zypper)."
msgstr "ການອັບເດດ instance ຂອງ {productname} ສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ຜ່ານແຊນແນວເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນໂດຍໃຊ້ເຄື່ອງມືມາດຕະຖານຂອງ SUSE (ເຊັ່ນ: zypper)."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "Is the use of {productname} Hub supported with this listing?"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ {productname} Hub ແມ່ນຮອງຮັບໃນລາຍການນີ້ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:21
msgid ""
"Yes, {productname} Hub is recommended for customers with more than 10,000 "
"managed clients. If the {productname} Hub instance has no connected clients, "
"there will be no charge for the {productname} Hub software components."
msgstr "ໄດ້, {productname} Hub ແມ່ນແນະນຳສຳລັບລູກຄ້າທີ່ມີໄຄລແອນຫຼາຍກວ່າ 10,000 ເຄື່ອງ. ຫາກ {productname} Hub instance ບໍ່ມີໄຄລແອນເຊື່ອມຕໍ່, ຈະບໍ່ມີຄ່າບໍລິການສຳລັບຄອມໂພເນັນຊອບແວຂອງ Hub."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:22
msgid ""
"Billing will occur from the downstream {productname} {payg} Server instance, "
"where managed instances are connected."
msgstr "ການເກັບເງິນຈະເກີດຂຶ້ນຈາກ {productname} {payg} Server ທີ່ຢູ່ປາຍທາງ (downstream), ບ່ອນທີ່ມີ instance ເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ຢູ່."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:23
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Can I manage {byoslongform} - {byos} SLES instances in the cloud with "
"{productname} {payg}?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍສາມາດຈັດການອິນສະແຕນຊ໌ SLES ແບບ {byoslongform} - {byos} ໃນຄລາວດ້ວຍ {productname} {payg} ໄດ້ຫຼືບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:24
msgid ""
"To manage {byos} instances, {scclongform} ({scc}) credentials with "
"entitlement to valid SLES or SLES for SAP subscriptions will be "
"required. These credentials should be added to the {productname} "
"configuration to enable this functionality."
msgstr "ໃນການຈັດການ {byos} instances, ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງມີຂໍ້ມູນປະຈຳຕົວ {scclongform} ({scc}) ທີ່ມີສິດການນຳໃຊ້ SLES ຫຼື SLES for SAP. ຂໍ້ມູນເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຕ້ອງຖືກເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໃນການກຳນົດຄ່າຂອງ {productname} ເພື່ອເປີດໃຊ້ງານ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I have a hybrid setup. Can I manage instances (workloads) outside of the "
"cloud?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍມີການຕັ້ງຄ່າແບບໄຮບຣິດ (hybrid). ຂ້ອຍສາມາດຈັດການ instance (workloads) ທີ່ຢູ່ນອກ cloud ໄດ້ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:26
msgid "Yes, it is possible to manage instances, in the cloud, on premises or both."
msgstr "ໄດ້, ເຈົ້າສາມາດຈັດການ instance ໄດ້ທັງໃນ cloud, on-premises ຫຼື ທັງສອງຢ່າງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:27
msgid ""
"To enable management of SUSE workloads in an on-premises data center, {scc} "
"credentials with entitlement to valid SLES or SLES for SAP subscriptions "
"will be required."
msgstr "ເພື່ອເປີດການຈັດການ SUSE workloads ໃນ on-premises data center, ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງມີຂໍ້ມູນປະຈຳຕົວ {scc} ທີ່ມີສິດການນຳໃຊ້ SLES ຫຼື SLES for SAP."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:28
msgid ""
"These credentials should be added to the {productname} configuration to "
"enable this functionality."
msgstr "ຂໍ້ມູນປະຈຳຕົວເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຄວນຖືກເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໃນການກຳນົດຄ່າ {productname} ເພື່ອເປີດໃຊ້ງານ."

#. type: delimited block =
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" Egress data charges may apply when managing workloads outside of the cloud "
"provider's network.\n"
msgstr " ອາດມີຄ່າບໍລິການຂໍ້ມູນຂາອອກ (Egress data) ເມື່ອຈັດການ workloads ທີ່ຢູ່ນອກເຄືອຂ່າຍຂອງຜູ້ໃຫ້ບໍລິການ cloud.\n"

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:30
#, no-wrap
msgid "Are there additional charges for using a {productname} Proxy?"
msgstr "ມີຄ່າບໍລິການເພີ່ມເຕີມໃນການໃຊ້ {productname} Proxy ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:31
msgid ""
"With a hybrid landscape, egress data charges may apply when managing "
"workloads outside of the cloud provider. To reduce these costs, SUSE "
"recommend the use of the containerized proxy."
msgstr "ໃນສະພາບແວດລ້ອມແບບໄຮບຣິດ, ອາດມີຄ່າ Egress data. ເພື່ອຫຼຸດຄ່າໃຊ້ຈ່າຍເຫຼົ່ານີ້, SUSE ແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ containerized proxy."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:32
msgid ""
"Please note: Whilst the SUSE Manger Proxy usage is included as part of the "
"{productname} {payg} subscription, an LCM+ subscription will be billed if "
"the proxy is also a managed workload, so in other words it counted as a "
"managed client."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Can I have a {productname} {payg} Server on premises and bill via the Cloud "
"Marketplace?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍສາມາດມີ {productname} {payg} Server ແບບ on-premises ແລ້ວໃຫ້ເກັບເງິນຜ່ານ Cloud Marketplace ໄດ້ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:34
msgid ""
"No, to benefit from cloud marketplace billing, the {productname} {payg} "
"instance must reside on the cloud. Any {productname} instances on premises "
"will require their own subscriptions."
msgstr "ບໍ່ໄດ້, ເພື່ອໃຫ້ສາມາດເກັບເງິນຜ່ານ cloud marketplace, {productname} {payg} instance ຕ້ອງຢູ່ໃນ cloud ເທົ່ານັ້ນ. instance ໃດໆທີ່ຢູ່ on-premises ຈະຕ້ອງໃຊ້ການສະໝັກໃຊ້ຂອງຕົນເອງ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "What client Operating Systems are supported with {productname} {payg}?"
msgstr "ລະບົບປະຕິບັດການໄຄລແອນໃດແດ່ທີ່ຮອງຮັບໃນ {productname} {payg}?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-products.adoc:36
msgid ""
"Please refer to the product documentation for a full list of supported "
"clients.  "
"link:https://documentation.suse.com/suma/4.3/ja/suse-manager/specialized-guides/public-cloud-guide/payg/payg-overview.html[{payg} "
"Overview]"
msgstr "ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງເອກະສານຜະລິດຕະພັນສຳລັບລາຍຊື່ໄຄລແອນທີ່ຮອງຮັບທັງໝົດ. link:https://documentation.suse.com/suma/4.3/ja/suse-manager/specialized-guides/public-cloud-guide/payg/payg-overview.html[ພາບລວມ {payg}]"

#. type: Title =
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Billing - Technical"
msgstr "ການຄິດໄລ່ຄ່າບໍລິການ - ເຕັກນິກ"

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Do I need any special or additional infrastructure to set up {productname} "
"billing via the cloud marketplaces?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍຕ້ອງມີໂຄງລ່າງພື້ນຖານພິເສດ ຫຼື ເພີ່ມເຕີມເພື່ອຕັ້ງຄ່າການເກັບເງິນ {productname} ຜ່ານ cloud marketplaces ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:4
msgid ""
"No, all components needed to handle the billing are part of the "
"{productname} {payg} code base."
msgstr "ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນ, ທຸກຄອມໂພເນັນທີ່ຈຳເປັນໃນການຈັດການການເກັບເງິນແມ່ນເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງ {productname} {payg} ຢູ່ແລ້ວ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What is the deployment mechanism for {productname} {payg} on the cloud "
"marketplace?"
msgstr "ກົນໄກການວາງລະບົບ {productname} {payg} ໃນ cloud marketplace ແມ່ນຫຍັງ?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:6
msgid ""
"The cloud marketplace listing for {productname} {payg} will deploy a "
"{productname} instance, together with the embedded billing engine."
msgstr "ລາຍການໃນ cloud marketplace ສຳລັບ {productname} {payg} ຈະທຳການວາງລະບົບ {productname} instance ພ້ອມກັບລະບົບການເກັບເງິນທີ່ຕິດຕົ່ວມາ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What version of {productname} is installed when using the marketplace "
"listing?"
msgstr "ເມື່ອໃຊ້ລາຍການໃນ marketplace, {productname} ເວີຊັນໃດຈະຖືກຕິດຕັ້ງ?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:8
msgid ""
"The cloud marketplace listing for {productname} {payg} is tied to a specific "
"version of {productname} (4.3.8 at launch).  Future listings will typically "
"include the latest version available at the time of product/image "
"creation. Please check the listing for further information."
msgstr "ລາຍການໃນ cloud marketplace ສຳລັບ {productname} {payg} ຈະຜູກກັບເວີຊັນສະເພາະ (ເຊັ່ນ 4.3.8 ຕອນເປີດຕົວ). ລາຍການໃນອະນາຄົດຈະລວມເອົາເວີຊັນຫຼ້າສຸດທີ່ມີໃນເວລານັ້ນ. ກະລຸນາກວດສອບລາຍລະອຽດໃນ marketplace ຕື່ມ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:9
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I need a prior version of {productname} installed; can I still use the "
"listing?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍຕ້ອງການຕິດຕັ້ງ {productname} ເວີຊັນກ່ອນໜ້ານີ້; ຂ້ອຍຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ລາຍການນີ້ໄດ້ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:10
msgid ""
"No, there is no choice over the {productname} version when deploying using "
"the cloud marketplace listing. If a prior version of {productname} is "
"required, this will need to be installed manually using the standard "
"documentation and {byos} billing."
msgstr "ບໍ່ໄດ້, ເຈົ້າບໍ່ສາມາດເລືອກເວີຊັນຂອງ {productname} ໄດ້ເມື່ອວາງລະບົບຜ່ານ cloud marketplace. ຫາກຕ້ອງການເວີຊັນກ່ອນໜ້ານີ້, ເຈົ້າຕ້ອງຕິດຕັ້ງດ້ວຍຕົນເອງໂດຍໃຊ້ເອກະສານມາດຕະຖານ ແລະ ການເກັບເງິນແບບ {byos}."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:11
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"How often is the listing updated (including the version of {productname} "
"etc.)?"
msgstr "ລາຍການໃນ marketplace ມີການອັບເດດເລື້ອຍປານໃດ (ລວມເຖິງເວີຊັນຂອງ {productname} ແລະ ອື່ນໆ)?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:12
msgid ""
"The Marketplace listing is tied to a specific version of {productname}, "
"which is the latest version available at the time of the listing."
msgstr "ລາຍການໃນ Marketplace ຈະຜູກກັບເວີຊັນສະເພາະຂອງ {productname}, ເຊິ່ງເປັນເວີຊັນຫຼ້າສຸດທີ່ມີໃນຕອນທີ່ລົງລາຍການ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:13
msgid ""
"Typically, the listing in the cloud marketplace is updated quarterly, or "
"more frequently if there are security issues."
msgstr "ໂດຍປົກກະຕິ, ລາຍການໃນ cloud marketplace ຈະຖືກອັບເດດທຸກໆໄຕມາດ, ຫຼື ເລື້ອຍກວ່າຫາກມີບັນຫາດ້ານຄວາມປອດໄພ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:14
msgid ""
"It is worth noting that the image update process may not be fully aligned to "
"the {productname} product maintenance releases (every 6-8 weeks), so "
"{productname} {payg} instances should be patched regularly after deployment."
msgstr "ຄວນສັງເກດວ່າຂະບວນການອັບເດດອິເມຈອາດຈະບໍ່ຕົງກັບຮອບການປ່ອຍຕົວບຳລຸງຮັກສາ (ທຸກໆ 6-8 ອາທິດ), ດັ່ງນັ້ນ {productname} {payg} instance ຄວນໄດ້ຮັບການລົງແພັດ (patch) ຢ່າງສະໝໍ່າສະເໝີຫຼັງຈາກວາງລະບົບແລ້ວ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I have purchased multiple {payg} - {payglongform} SUSE products from the "
"cloud provider marketplace (i.e. Rancher, NeuVector and {productname}), does "
"the marketplace billing method still work?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍໄດ້ຊື້ຜະລິດຕະພັນ SUSE ແບບ {payg} - {payglongform} ຫຼາຍລາຍການຈາກຕະຫຼາດຂອງຜູ້ໃຫ້ບໍລິການຄລາວ (ເຊັ່ນ: Rancher, NeuVector ແລະ {productname}), ວິທີການຮຽກເກັບເງິນຂອງຕະຫຼາດຍັງໃຊ້ງານໄດ້ຢູ່ຫຼືບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:16
msgid ""
"Yes, the billing mechanism for the products is independent. Each deployment "
"will be billed separately via the cloud marketplace."
msgstr "ໄດ້, ກົນໄກການເກັບເງິນສຳລັບແຕ່ລະຜະລິດຕະພັນແມ່ນແຍກຈາກກັນ. ແຕ່ລະການວາງລະບົບຈະຖືກເກັບເງິນແຍກກັນຜ່ານ cloud marketplace."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"I already have an existing {productname} deployment; how can I get this "
"deployment to bill via the cloud marketplace?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍມີການວາງລະບົບ {productname} ຢູ່ແລ້ວ; ຂ້ອຍຈະປ່ຽນໃຫ້ມັນເກັບເງິນຜ່ານ cloud marketplace ໄດ້ແນວໃດ?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-billing-technical.adoc:18
msgid ""
"Existing deployments *cannot* be directly converted or updated to provide "
"billing via the cloud marketplace. To benefit from monthly billing, "
"{productname} {payg} must be deployed directly from the cloud marketplace "
"listing."
msgstr "ການວາງລະບົບທີ່ມີຢູ່ *ບໍ່ສາມາດ* ປ່ຽນ ຫຼື ອັບເດດໃຫ້ເປັນແບບເກັບເງິນຜ່ານ cloud marketplace ໄດ້ໂດຍກົງ. ເພື່ອໃຊ້ປະໂຫຍດຈາກການເກັບເງິນລາຍເດືອນ, {productname} {payg} ຕ້ອງຖືກວາງລະບົບໂດຍກົງຈາກລາຍການໃນ cloud marketplace ເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#. type: Title =
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Public Cloud Listings"
msgstr "ລາຍການຄລາວສາທາລະນະ"

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "What is the {productname} {payg} listing on the cloud marketplaces?"
msgstr "ລາຍການ {productname} {payg} ໃນຕະຫຼາດຄລາວ (Cloud Marketplaces) ແມ່ນຫຍັງ?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:4
msgid ""
"By selecting the {productname} {payg} listing from the cloud marketplace, "
"customers can deploy {productname} to their cloud environment with the "
"advantage of having monthly billing via the cloud provider."
msgstr "ໂດຍການເລືອກລາຍການ {productname} {payg} ຈາກຕະຫຼາດຄລາວ, ລູກຄ້າສາມາດຕິດຕັ້ງ {productname} ລົງໃນສະພາບແວດລ້ອມຄລາວຂອງຕົນເອງ ໂດຍມີຂໍ້ດີຄືການຄິດໄລ່ເງິນເປັນລາຍເດືອນຜ່ານຜູ້ໃຫ້ບໍລິການຄລາວ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:5
msgid ""
"Customers still have the option of using {productname} {byos} "
"({byoslongform}), for which subscriptions and billing is handled directly by "
"{suse}."
msgstr "ລູກຄ້າຍັງມີທາງເລືອກໃນການນຳໃຊ້ {productname} {byos} ({byoslongform}), ເຊິ່ງການສະໝັກໃຊ້ ແລະ ການຄິດໄລ່ເງິນຈະຖືກຈັດການໂດຍ {suse} ໂດຍກົງ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Where do I find the {productname} {payg} listings?"
msgstr "ຂ້ອຍສາມາດຊອກຫາລາຍການ {productname} {payg} ໄດ້ຢູ່ໃສ?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:7
msgid ""
"The listings can be found in the {availability} Marketplaces.  There are two "
"listings:"
msgstr "ສາມາດຊອກຫາລາຍການເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໄດ້ໃນຕະຫຼາດ {availability} (Marketplaces) ເຊິ່ງມີຢູ່ສອງລາຍການຄື:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:8
msgid "On the {aws} Marketplace, you will find the following:"
msgstr "ໃນ {aws} Marketplace, ທ່ານຈະພົບເຫັນລາຍການດັ່ງນີ້:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:9
msgid "{productname} Server Family (Non-EU and non-UK only)"
msgstr "{productname} Server Family (ສະເພາະນອກ EU ແລະ ນອກ UK ເທົ່ານັ້ນ)"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:10
msgid "{productname} Server Family (EU and UK only)"
msgstr "{productname} Server Family (ສະເພາະ EU ແລະ UK ເທົ່ານັ້ນ)"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:11
msgid "On the {azure} Marketplace, you will find:"
msgstr "ໃນ {azure} Marketplace, ທ່ານຈະພົບເຫັນ:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:12
msgid "{productname} with 24x7 Support"
msgstr "{productname} ພ້ອມການສະໜັບສະໜູນ 24x7"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:13
msgid "{productname} with 24x7 Support (EMEA Orders Only)"
msgstr "{productname} ພ້ອມການສະໜັບສະໜູນ 24x7 (ສະເພາະການສັ່ງຊື້ໃນ EMEA ເທົ່ານັ້ນ)"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:14
msgid ""
"For the purposes of this FAQ, we will refer to these listings as "
"{productname} {payg}."
msgstr "ເພື່ອຈຸດປະສົງຂອງ FAQ ນີ້, ພວກເຮົາຈະເອີ້ນລາຍການເຫຼົ່ານີ້ວ່າ {productname} {payg}."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why are there 2 listings and which one should I use?"
msgstr "ເປັນຫຍັງຈຶ່ງມີ 2 ລາຍການ ແລະ ຂ້ອຍຄວນໃຊ້ລາຍການໃດ?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:16
msgid "We have 2 listings for {productname}:"
msgstr "ພວກເຮົາມີ 2 ລາຍການສຳລັບ {productname}:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:17
#, no-wrap
msgid "**EU and UK only / EMEA Orders Only** \n"
msgstr "**ສະເພາະ EU ແລະ UK / ສະເພາະການສັ່ງຊື້ໃນ EMEA ເທົ່ານັ້ນ** \n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:18
#, no-wrap
msgid "**non-EU and non-UK only**.\n"
msgstr "**ສະເພາະນອກ EU ແລະ ນອກ UK ເທົ່ານັ້ນ**.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:19
msgid ""
"You should pick the listing that reflects in which country your "
"{availability} account gets billed."
msgstr "ທ່ານຄວນເລືອກລາຍການທີ່ກົງກັບປະເທດທີ່ບັນຊີ {availability} ຂອງທ່ານຖືກຄິດໄລ່ເງິນ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:20
#, no-wrap
msgid "Are these listings available in all countries?"
msgstr "ລາຍການເຫຼົ່ານີ້ມີໃຫ້ບໍລິການໃນທຸກປະເທດບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:21
msgid ""
"The {productname} {payg} listing on the cloud is not available to purchase "
"in all countries.  In case it is not available in your country you can still "
"use the {byos} option."
msgstr "ລາຍການ {productname} {payg} ເທິງຄລາວບໍ່ມີໃຫ້ຊື້ໃນທຸກປະເທດ. ໃນກໍລະນີທີ່ບໍ່ມີໃຫ້ບໍລິການໃນປະເທດຂອງທ່ານ, ທ່ານຍັງສາມາດໃຊ້ທາງເລືອກ {byos} ໄດ້."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:22
msgid ""
"Your billing country is based on the {availability} Account ID used to do "
"the deployment."
msgstr "ປະເທດທີ່ຄິດໄລ່ເງິນຂອງທ່ານແມ່ນອີງຕາມ ID ບັນຊີ {availability} ທີ່ໃຊ້ໃນການຕິດຕັ້ງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:23
msgid "You can find out more about confirming your tax location as follows:"
msgstr "ທ່ານສາມາດສຶກສາເພີ່ມເຕີມກ່ຽວກັບການຢືນຢັນສະຖານທີ່ເສຍພາສີໄດ້ດັ່ງນີ້:"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:24
msgid ""
"For Amazon Web Services, it depends on the *tax address* of the account, see "
"link:https://aws.amazon.com/tax-help/location[Tax help based on location]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:25
msgid ""
"For Microsoft Azure, it depends on the *sold to* address of the account, see "
"link:https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/cost-management-billing/manage/change-azure-account-profile[Azure "
"account profile]"
msgstr ""

#. * For Google Cloud, it depends on the *billing country* of the account, see link:https://support.google.com/cloudidentity/answer/3530790[Google support answer]
#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:26
msgid ""
"Please see the link at the end of this FAQ for a list of countries that can "
"and cannot transact {productname} {payg} via the cloud marketplaces."
msgstr "ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງລິ້ງຢູ່ທ້າຍ FAQ ນີ້ ສຳລັບລາຍຊື່ປະເທດທີ່ສາມາດ ແລະ ບໍ່ສາມາດ ເຮັດທຸລະກຳ {productname} {payg} ຜ່ານຕະຫຼາດຄລາວໄດ້."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:27
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"My cloud account is in the USA, but I want to deploy {productname} {payg} in "
"another region, a region that is in a country where I currently cannot "
"transact, is this possible?"
msgstr "ບັນຊີຄລາວຂອງຂ້ອຍຢູ່ໃນ USA, ແຕ່ຂ້ອຍຕ້ອງການຕິດຕັ້ງ {productname} {payg} ໃນພາກພື້ນ (Region) ອື່ນ ເຊິ່ງເປັນປະເທດທີ່ຂ້ອຍບໍ່ສາມາດເຮັດທຸລະກຳໄດ້ໃນຕອນນີ້, ມັນສາມາດເຮັດໄດ້ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:28
msgid ""
"If your cloud provider account is billed to one of the allowed countries, it "
"is possible to deploy {productname} in any region."
msgstr "ຫາກບັນຊີຜູ້ໃຫ້ບໍລິການຄລາວຂອງທ່ານຖືກຄິດໄລ່ເງິນໃນປະເທດໃດໜຶ່ງທີ່ໄດ້ຮັບອະນຸຍາດ, ທ່ານກໍສາມາດຕິດຕັ້ງ {productname} ໃນພາກພື້ນໃດກໍໄດ້."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:29
#, no-wrap
msgid "Is this listing available in China?"
msgstr "ລາຍການນີ້ມີໃຫ້ບໍລິການໃນປະເທດຈີນບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:30
msgid ""
"It is not possible to transact/bill {productname} {payg} via {availability} "
"Marketplaces in China.  It is possible to deploy into regions in China."
msgstr "ບໍ່ສາມາດເຮັດທຸລະກຳ ຫຼື ຄິດໄລ່ເງິນ {productname} {payg} ຜ່ານ {availability} Marketplaces ໃນປະເທດຈີນໄດ້. ແຕ່ສາມາດຕິດຕັ້ງລົງໃນພາກພື້ນຕ່າງໆໃນປະເທດຈີນໄດ້."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:31
msgid ""
"This means you can deploy {productname} in a region in China if your billing "
"is performed in a country that has the {payg} option available.  Please see "
"the addendum at the end of this FAQ for a list of countries that can and "
"cannot transact {productname} {payg} via the cloud."
msgstr "ນີ້ໝາຍຄວາມວ່າທ່ານສາມາດຕິດຕັ້ງ {productname} ໃນພາກພື້ນຂອງຈີນໄດ້ ຫາກການຄິດໄລ່ເງິນຂອງທ່ານ ເຮັດຢູ່ໃນປະເທດທີ່ມີທາງເລືອກ {payg} ໃຫ້ບໍລິການ. ກະລຸນາເບິ່ງເອກະສານເພີ່ມເຕີມຢູ່ທ້າຍ FAQ ນີ້ ສຳລັບລາຍຊື່ປະເທດທີ່ສາມາດ ແລະ ບໍ່ສາມາດເຮັດທຸລະກຳ {productname} {payg} ຜ່ານຄລາວໄດ້."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:32
#, no-wrap
msgid "Is there still a {byos} listing for {productname} in the marketplace?"
msgstr "ຍັງມີລາຍການ {byos} ສຳລັບ {productname} ໃນຕະຫຼາດ (Marketplace) ຢູ່ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:33
msgid ""
"Yes, for customers that wish to use an existing annual {productname} "
"subscription, the {byos} {productname} listing is available."
msgstr "ມີ, ສຳລັບລູກຄ້າທີ່ຕ້ອງການໃຊ້ການສະໝັກໃຊ້ລາຍປີທີ່ມີຢູ່ແລ້ວຂອງ {productname}, ລາຍການ {byos} {productname} ແມ່ນມີໃຫ້ບໍລິການ."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:34
#, no-wrap
msgid "Is there a {payg} listing available for the {productname} Proxy Server?"
msgstr "ມີລາຍການ {payg} ສຳລັບ {productname} Proxy Server ບໍ່?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:35
msgid ""
"If a {productname} Proxy is required as part of the architecture, it is "
"suggested to use the containerized proxy.  See the SUSE documentation at: "
"link:https://documentation.suse.com[documentation.suse.com]"
msgstr "ຫາກຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງມີ {productname} Proxy ເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງໂຄງສ້າງ, ແນະນຳໃຫ້ໃຊ້ containerized proxy. ເບິ່ງເອກະສານຂອງ SUSE ໄດ້ທີ່: link:https://documentation.suse.com[documentation.suse.com]"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:36
msgid ""
"menu:Select[{productname} > {productname} {{productnumber}} > Installation "
"and Upgrade guide > Installation > {productname} Proxy > Install "
"Containerized Proxy]"
msgstr "ເມນູ:Select[{productname} > {productname} {{productnumber}} > Installation and Upgrade guide > Installation > {productname} Proxy > Install Containerized Proxy]"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:37
msgid ""
"From the subscription point of view, {productname} Proxy is a managed "
"client."
msgstr "ໃນມຸມມອງຂອງການສະໝັກໃຊ້, {productname} Proxy ຖືວ່າເປັນລູກຂ່າຍທີ່ຖືກຈັດການ (Managed client)."

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The listing shows pricing information for {productname} node management and "
"a separate price for monitoring. Do I need to subscribe twice if I need "
"monitoring?"
msgstr "ລາຍການສະແດງຂໍ້ມູນລາຄາສຳລັບການຈັດການໂນດ {productname} ແລະ ລາຄາແຍກຕ່າງຫາກສຳລັບການຕິດຕາມ (Monitoring). ຂ້ອຍຕ້ອງສະໝັກໃຊ້ສອງຄັ້ງບໍ່ ຫາກຕ້ອງການໃຊ້ການຕິດຕາມນຳ?"

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:39
msgid ""
"There is no need to subscribe twice.  Subscribing to the listing in the "
"cloud provider marketplace allow the {productname} {payg} instance to "
"perform metered billing for {productname} usage."
msgstr "ບໍ່ຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງສະໝັກໃຊ້ສອງຄັ້ງ. ການສະໝັກໃຊ້ລາຍການໃນຕະຫຼາດຂອງຜູ້ໃຫ້ບໍລິການຄລາວ ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ອິນສະແຕນຊ໌ (Instance) ຂອງ {productname} {payg} ສາມາດຄິດໄລ່ເງິນຕາມປະລິມານການໃຊ້ງານ {productname} ຕົວຈິງ."

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-listings.adoc:40
msgid ""
"If you onboard an instance and enable {productname} monitoring, there is a "
"monthly charge for management and another charge for monitoring."
msgstr "ຫາກທ່ານເພີ່ມອິນສະແຕນຊ໌ ແລະ ເປີດໃຊ້ການຕິດຕາມຂອງ {productname}, ຈະມີຄ່າບໍລິການລາຍເດືອນສຳລັບການຈັດການ ແລະ ອີກສ່ວນໜຶ່ງສຳລັບການຕິດຕາມ."

#. type: Title =
#: modules/specialized-guides/pages/public-cloud-guide/faq/faq-miscellaneous.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Miscellaneous"
msgstr "ອື່ນໆ"

